WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:26.878
Mama!

3
00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:36.679
Mama!

4
00:01:42.644 --> 00:01:43.978
Mama!

5
00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:52.003
Mother. What are you...

6
00:02:52.088 --> 00:02:54.423
I thought you were a burglar.

7
00:02:54.508 --> 00:02:55.925
I didn't mean to
scare you. darling.

8
00:02:55.925 --> 00:02:57.384
I was just getting a snack.

9
00:02:57.593 --> 00:02:59.637
Go back to bed.

10
00:03:00.597 --> 00:03:02.473
What's the matter?

11
00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:04.933
Go on. back to bed.

12
00:03:06.562 --> 00:03:08.478
I'll make you a hot chocolate.

13
00:03:09.313 --> 00:03:10.438
Who are you?

14
00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:16.987
And what have you
done with my mother?

15
00:03:17.155 --> 00:03:21.324
My mother has never set
foot in this kitchen in her life.

16
00:03:21.993 --> 00:03:25.204
And she certainly never
made me a hot chocolate.

17
00:03:25.454 --> 00:03:28.123
Unless you count ordering
the maid to do it.

18
00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:48.311
You're not scared of me?

19
00:03:48.687 --> 00:03:51.896
I always believed I couldn't
be the only one in the world.

20
00:03:52.566 --> 00:03:54.317
The only person who was

21
00:03:55.026 --> 00:03:56.485
different.

22
00:03:57.778 --> 00:03:59.280
And here you are.

23
00:03:59.823 --> 00:04:01.073
Charles Xavier.

24
00:04:04.328 --> 00:04:05.661
Raven.

25
00:04:06.830 --> 00:04:08.622
You're hungry and alone.

26
00:04:08.998 --> 00:04:10.498
Take whatever you want.

27
00:04:10.626 --> 00:04:14.044
We've got lots of food.
You don't have to steal.

28
00:04:14.462 --> 00:04:16.963
In fact.

29
00:04:17.048 --> 00:04:18.841
you never have to steal again.

30
00:04:33.398 --> 00:04:35.483
Understand this. Erik...

31
00:04:36.526 --> 00:04:39.403
These Nazis. I'm not like them.

32
00:04:43.742 --> 00:04:46.034
Genes are the key. yes?

33
00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:49.288
But their goals?

34
00:04:49.372 --> 00:04:53.834
Blue eyes? Blond hair? Pathetic.

35
00:04:55.879 --> 00:04:57.088
Mmm!

36
00:04:59.382 --> 00:05:00.925
Eat the chocolate.

37
00:05:01.968 --> 00:05:03.009
It's good.

38
00:05:03.803 --> 00:05:04.845
Want some?

39
00:05:07.391 --> 00:05:09.141
I want to see my mama.

40
00:05:15.981 --> 00:05:21.403
Genes are the key that unlocks
the door to a new age. Erik.

41
00:05:22.197 --> 00:05:25.490
A new future for mankind.

42
00:05:25.951 --> 00:05:28.661
Evolution.

43
00:05:28.745 --> 00:05:30.829
You know what I'm talking about?

44
00:05:32.374 --> 00:05:35.918
It's a simple thing I ask of you.

45
00:05:36.211 --> 00:05:41.005
A little coin is nothing
compared to a big gate.

46
00:05:42.425 --> 00:05:43.591
Is it?

47
00:05:52.978 --> 00:05:55.062
Ja.

48
00:05:58.649 --> 00:06:00.567
I tried. herr doctor.

49
00:06:00.735 --> 00:06:04.904
I can't... I don't...

50
00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:06.656
It's impossible.

51
00:06:09.494 --> 00:06:11.495
The one thing I can
say for the Nazis

52
00:06:11.579 --> 00:06:14.372
is their methods seem
to produce results.

53
00:06:17.711 --> 00:06:19.252
I'm sorry. Erik.

54
00:06:30.264 --> 00:06:31.473
Mama!

55
00:06:32.391 --> 00:06:33.683
My darling.

56
00:06:34.644 --> 00:06:35.685
How are you?

57
00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:41.149
Here's what we're going to do.

58
00:06:42.569 --> 00:06:44.444
I'm going to count to three...

59
00:06:45.988 --> 00:06:48.365
And you're going to move the coin.

60
00:06:49.576 --> 00:06:53.454
You don't move the coin.
I pull the trigger.

61
00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:57.415
Understand?

62
00:06:59.084 --> 00:07:00.877
One.

63
00:07:01.504 --> 00:07:02.504
Mama.

64
00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:03.755
You can do it.

65
00:07:08.762 --> 00:07:10.053
Two.

66
00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:14.350
Everything is all right.

67
00:07:30.742 --> 00:07:31.783
Three.

68
00:07:53.223 --> 00:07:55.014
Yes. Wonderful.

69
00:08:05.110 --> 00:08:06.110
Excellent.

70
00:08:17.413 --> 00:08:20.875
Nein!

71
00:08:50.654 --> 00:08:52.280
Outstanding. Erik.

72
00:08:53.616 --> 00:08:57.161
So we unlock your gift with anger.

73
00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:01.624
Anger and pain.

74
00:09:04.251 --> 00:09:05.878
You and me...

75
00:09:07.087 --> 00:09:09.965
We're going to have a
lot of fun together.

76
00:10:23.248 --> 00:10:25.416
Heterochromia.

77
00:10:27.085 --> 00:10:29.628
A gentleman would at least
offer to buy me a drink first.

78
00:10:30.379 --> 00:10:34.298
Norman. a pint of bitter for
me and a Brandy for the lady. please.

79
00:10:34.384 --> 00:10:35.842
How did you know that?
Lucky guess.

80
00:10:36.177 --> 00:10:38.011
My name is Xavier.
Charles Xavier.

81
00:10:38.096 --> 00:10:39.303
How do you do? Amy.

82
00:10:39.389 --> 00:10:41.306
Heterochromia was in
reference to your eyes.

83
00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:43.892
which I have to say are stunning.

84
00:10:43.976 --> 00:10:45.601
One green. one blue.

85
00:10:45.854 --> 00:10:47.895
It's a mutation. It's a
very groovy mutation.

86
00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.523
I've got news for you. Amy.

87
00:10:49.606 --> 00:10:51.191
You are a mutant.

88
00:10:51.484 --> 00:10:52.817
First you proposition a girl.

89
00:10:52.902 --> 00:10:54.945
and then you call her deformed.

90
00:10:55.029 --> 00:10:57.155
How is that seduction
technique working for you?

91
00:10:57.240 --> 00:10:58.399
I'll tell you in the morning.

92
00:10:59.158 --> 00:11:01.576
No. seriously.
though. you mustn't knock it.

93
00:11:01.660 --> 00:11:03.453
Mutation took us from
single-celled organisms

94
00:11:03.538 --> 00:11:06.956
to being the dominant form of
reproductive life on this planet.

95
00:11:07.042 --> 00:11:10.168
Infinite forms of variation
with each generation.

96
00:11:10.253 --> 00:11:12.921
all through mutation.

97
00:11:14.256 --> 00:11:15.923
Then let's reclaim that word.

98
00:11:20.221 --> 00:11:22.514
Mutant and proud.
Chin-chin. Hey.

99
00:11:22.599 --> 00:11:24.099
I guess I have to buy my own drink.

100
00:11:24.183 --> 00:11:25.308
I'm sorry. One cola.

101
00:11:25.769 --> 00:11:26.851
Charles here was just telling me

102
00:11:26.936 --> 00:11:29.354
that I'm like one of the first
sea creatures that grew legs.

103
00:11:29.438 --> 00:11:31.398
A tiny bit sexier.

104
00:11:31.482 --> 00:11:34.485
I'm sorry. This is
my sister. raven.

105
00:11:34.568 --> 00:11:35.818
Hi. Amy.

106
00:11:36.111 --> 00:11:38.447
And what do you study?
Waitressing.

107
00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:39.740
Ah.

108
00:11:42.951 --> 00:11:44.536
Oh. look. you have
heterochromia. too.

109
00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:47.538
Sorry. what? Look at her eye.

110
00:11:50.418 --> 00:11:52.961
Right. Raven. get
your coat. please.

111
00:11:53.462 --> 00:11:55.129
Don't talk to me.
You did that on purpose.

112
00:11:55.215 --> 00:11:57.341
I did not! Why would I do it
on purpose? Yes. you did!

113
00:11:57.424 --> 00:11:59.759
You know I can't control it
sometimes if I'm stressed or tired.

114
00:11:59.844 --> 00:12:02.763
You seem to be doing a
perfectly good job right now.

115
00:12:02.846 --> 00:12:04.639
"Mutant and proud." What?

116
00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:06.307
Or is it only with
pretty mutations.

117
00:12:06.392 --> 00:12:08.184
or invisible ones like yours?

118
00:12:08.269 --> 00:12:09.812
But if you're a freak.
you better hide.

119
00:12:09.895 --> 00:12:12.063
You're being ridiculous.

120
00:12:12.148 --> 00:12:14.232
I don't mean to sound
like an old fart.

121
00:12:14.317 --> 00:12:15.442
Which you are.

122
00:12:15.527 --> 00:12:16.652
Sometimes.

123
00:12:17.070 --> 00:12:19.488
But we've talked about this. raven.

124
00:12:19.572 --> 00:12:21.072
A small slip-up is one thing.

125
00:12:21.157 --> 00:12:22.990
A big one does not
bear thinking about.

126
00:12:29.124 --> 00:12:31.500
"Mutant and proud."

127
00:12:33.919 --> 00:12:36.087
"Mutant and proud"?

128
00:12:46.850 --> 00:12:48.350
If only.

129
00:12:54.315 --> 00:12:56.524
Would you date me?
Of course I would.

130
00:12:57.025 --> 00:12:59.903
Any young man would be lucky
to have you. You are stunning.

131
00:12:59.988 --> 00:13:01.113
Looking like this?

132
00:13:01.197 --> 00:13:03.197
Like... what?

133
00:13:06.619 --> 00:13:07.744
Blue?

134
00:13:10.539 --> 00:13:11.831
You're my oldest friend.

135
00:13:11.916 --> 00:13:13.375
I'm your only friend.

136
00:13:13.458 --> 00:13:14.876
Thank you for that.

137
00:13:15.419 --> 00:13:16.628
Well?

138
00:13:16.712 --> 00:13:18.963
I'm incapable of thinking
of you that way.

139
00:13:19.048 --> 00:13:20.215
I feel responsible for you.

140
00:13:20.884 --> 00:13:24.052
Anything else would
just feel wrong.

141
00:13:24.136 --> 00:13:25.386
But what if you didn't know me?

142
00:13:25.471 --> 00:13:26.638
Unfortunately. I do know you.

143
00:13:26.722 --> 00:13:28.139
I don't know what's
gotten into you lately.

144
00:13:28.224 --> 00:13:30.017
You're awfully concerned
with your looks.

145
00:13:34.813 --> 00:13:36.480
I'm sleepy.
Will you read to me?

146
00:13:36.566 --> 00:13:38.859
I can't. I have my thesis
coming up. I have to study.

147
00:13:38.942 --> 00:13:41.861
Fine. read that. Your thesis
always sends me right off.

148
00:13:42.404 --> 00:13:46.325
"To homo neanderthalensis. his
mutant cousin. homo sapiens."

149
00:13:46.408 --> 00:13:47.491
"was an aberration."

150
00:13:48.244 --> 00:13:52.581
"Peaceful cohabitation. if ever
it existed. was short-lived."

151
00:13:52.664 --> 00:13:54.124
"Records show.
without exception."

152
00:13:54.209 --> 00:13:57.336
"that the arrival of the mutated
human species in any region"

153
00:13:57.419 --> 00:13:59.587
"was followed by the
immediate extinction"

154
00:13:59.672 --> 00:14:02.381
"of their less-evolved kin."

155
00:14:08.222 --> 00:14:11.600
Possession of that gold is illegal.

156
00:14:11.683 --> 00:14:12.934
I should inform the police.

157
00:14:14.187 --> 00:14:15.394
Let's not play this game.

158
00:14:15.730 --> 00:14:17.438
Where did you get it?

159
00:14:18.357 --> 00:14:19.399
A friend.

160
00:14:19.692 --> 00:14:22.152
He recommended your
bank most highly.

161
00:14:24.113 --> 00:14:25.113
I see.

162
00:14:25.240 --> 00:14:27.615
Do you know our terms. sir?

163
00:14:28.158 --> 00:14:29.201
Yes.

164
00:14:30.827 --> 00:14:33.120
And you should know mine.

165
00:14:35.582 --> 00:14:38.418
This gold is what
remains of my people.

166
00:14:39.461 --> 00:14:40.879
Melted from their possessions.

167
00:14:40.963 --> 00:14:42.965
Torn from their teeth.

168
00:14:43.048 --> 00:14:44.966
This is blood money.

169
00:14:45.342 --> 00:14:48.135
And you're going to help me find
the bastards responsible for it.

170
00:14:53.809 --> 00:14:55.269
Don't touch that alarm.

171
00:14:58.022 --> 00:15:01.984
I want schmidt. Klaus schmidt.

172
00:15:02.067 --> 00:15:03.150
Where is he?

173
00:15:03.653 --> 00:15:05.861
Our clients don't provide
addresses. We're not...

174
00:15:05.947 --> 00:15:08.407
Not that sort of bank?

175
00:15:16.331 --> 00:15:17.791
Metal fillings. eh?

176
00:15:17.875 --> 00:15:18.875
Not gold.

177
00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:20.418
Worried someone
might steal them?

178
00:15:20.503 --> 00:15:23.713
Argentina! Schmidt
is in Argentina!

179
00:15:25.216 --> 00:15:28.927
Villa gesell! Please!

180
00:15:45.193 --> 00:15:46.193
Thank you.

181
00:15:50.658 --> 00:15:53.076
I would love to kill you.

182
00:15:57.123 --> 00:15:59.374
So mark my words.

183
00:15:59.459 --> 00:16:03.961
If you warn anyone I'm coming...

184
00:16:04.047 --> 00:16:05.714
I will find you.

185
00:16:18.311 --> 00:16:20.687
Another day
at the office.

186
00:16:20.772 --> 00:16:22.522
Is that
colonel hendry?

187
00:16:22.606 --> 00:16:23.981
<i>The NATO guy?</i>

188
00:16:24.067 --> 00:16:25.524
Yeah.

189
00:16:26.193 --> 00:16:27.818
Yes. it is.

190
00:16:27.903 --> 00:16:30.322
Because that's three mob
bosses. the Italian ambassador

191
00:16:30.405 --> 00:16:32.365
and the ceo of lockheed.

192
00:16:32.658 --> 00:16:34.326
They can't all be communists.

193
00:16:34.409 --> 00:16:36.870
This hellfire club. it's
got to be something else.

194
00:16:38.331 --> 00:16:40.915
Do you see that?

195
00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:43.085
Hello. girls.

196
00:16:43.168 --> 00:16:45.169
Wow! Very nice.

197
00:16:46.755 --> 00:16:48.255
What are you doing?

198
00:16:48.341 --> 00:16:52.094
<i>Using some equipment the CIA
didn't give me. Stay put.</i>

199
00:16:55.306 --> 00:16:57.224
Colonel hendry? Yes. ma'am.

200
00:16:57.432 --> 00:17:00.394
Emma frost. Sebastian
Shaw's associate.

201
00:17:01.437 --> 00:17:03.730
And where is Mr. Shaw?

202
00:17:03.815 --> 00:17:07.192
We're having a party. and
here's the entertainment.

203
00:17:07.276 --> 00:17:08.859
Come with me.

204
00:17:08.944 --> 00:17:11.613
Down like a roller coaster.

205
00:17:11.696 --> 00:17:14.031
Back like a loop-the-loop.

206
00:17:14.116 --> 00:17:17.201
And around like a
merry-go-round.

207
00:17:17.286 --> 00:17:19.871
We ate and ate at
a hot dog stand.

208
00:17:19.955 --> 00:17:21.355
We danced around to a rocking band.

209
00:17:23.209 --> 00:17:26.752
And when I could. I
gave that girl a hug.

210
00:17:26.837 --> 00:17:28.922
In the tunnel of love.

211
00:17:29.006 --> 00:17:31.298
You'll never know how
great a kiss can feel.

212
00:17:31.384 --> 00:17:34.051
When you stop at the
top of a Ferris wheel.

213
00:17:34.136 --> 00:17:38.013
When I fell in love
down at palisades park.

214
00:17:47.357 --> 00:17:48.983
Hello. beautiful. How are you?

215
00:17:49.109 --> 00:17:51.778
Hey. baby. You want to
find a quiet place?

216
00:17:51.863 --> 00:17:55.990
I am so sorry. I've been
booked by colonel hendry.

217
00:17:57.201 --> 00:17:58.742
Excuse me.

218
00:17:58.827 --> 00:18:00.244
We ate and ate at a hot dog stand.

219
00:18:00.328 --> 00:18:03.080
We danced around
to a rocking band.

220
00:18:03.165 --> 00:18:06.876
And when I could. I
gave that girl a hug.

221
00:18:06.961 --> 00:18:09.296
In the tunnel of love.

222
00:18:09.380 --> 00:18:11.381
You'll never know how
great a kiss can feel.

223
00:18:19.182 --> 00:18:21.474
You sure we can't get
you a refill. Bob?

224
00:18:21.558 --> 00:18:22.933
No.

225
00:18:23.019 --> 00:18:28.022
So. I hear you blocked the proposal to
position Jupiter missiles in Turkey.

226
00:18:30.192 --> 00:18:32.193
I expect you'll reconsider.

227
00:18:32.278 --> 00:18:34.028
We've had this conversation.

228
00:18:34.404 --> 00:18:38.240
You put our nukes in Turkey or
anywhere that close to Russia.

229
00:18:38.326 --> 00:18:40.117
and you're looking at war.

230
00:18:40.202 --> 00:18:41.702
Nuclear war.

231
00:19:14.694 --> 00:19:16.320
I don't ask for favors. colonel.

232
00:19:16.614 --> 00:19:19.074
I express my expectations.

233
00:19:19.282 --> 00:19:22.661
So. let me say it again.

234
00:19:22.744 --> 00:19:25.913
I expect you'll reconsider.

235
00:19:26.624 --> 00:19:28.959
The only thing I will reconsider

236
00:19:29.042 --> 00:19:32.253
is having another glass of
that delicious champagne.

237
00:19:44.599 --> 00:19:47.894
What the hell did you
put in my drink?

238
00:20:05.203 --> 00:20:08.123
You're thinking of running.
Hiding.

239
00:20:08.249 --> 00:20:10.125
We'd find you. hendry.

240
00:20:10.209 --> 00:20:13.044
There's not a fortress in the
world that could keep us out.

241
00:20:29.854 --> 00:20:32.730
Magnificent. Isn't she. Bob?

242
00:20:33.857 --> 00:20:37.986
Genetic mutation.
The evolution of the human genome.

243
00:20:38.069 --> 00:20:39.528
Where's azazel?

244
00:20:45.827 --> 00:20:47.429
Ah. We don't want the
colonel to be late.

245
00:20:51.375 --> 00:20:52.375
Comrade.

246
00:20:55.378 --> 00:20:58.088
Missiles in Turkey
send a very clear message.

247
00:20:58.173 --> 00:20:59.423
If we ever decide to fire them.

248
00:20:59.424 --> 00:21:00.467
the Russian early-warning system

249
00:21:00.550 --> 00:21:02.134
won't even have time to kick in.

250
00:21:02.219 --> 00:21:03.928
This better be
important. mactaggert.

251
00:21:04.012 --> 00:21:06.347
Whoa. slow down.

252
00:21:06.473 --> 00:21:08.767
Are you smoking them funny cigarettes?
People don't disappear.

253
00:21:08.851 --> 00:21:10.143
Colonel hendry was there.

254
00:21:10.227 --> 00:21:12.061
He was there. mccone.
in the hellfire club.

255
00:21:12.355 --> 00:21:13.646
Colonel hendry?

256
00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:15.773
I agree with you. general.

257
00:21:15.857 --> 00:21:17.317
I've reconsidered my position

258
00:21:17.401 --> 00:21:20.778
and I now believe we should put
Jupiter missiles in Turkey.

259
00:21:20.904 --> 00:21:22.071
Colonel hendry is here.

260
00:21:22.155 --> 00:21:25.450
So unless he magically traveled
3.000 Miles in the last 10 minutes.

261
00:21:25.534 --> 00:21:29.037
listen to me. I suggest that
you stop wasting my time.

262
00:21:29.121 --> 00:21:31.413
Looks like hendry wants
to start world war III.

263
00:21:31.499 --> 00:21:34.000
I got bigger things to deal
with right now. mactaggert.

264
00:21:34.085 --> 00:21:35.542
Sir. I...

265
00:21:35.670 --> 00:21:37.796
God!
Have you lost your mind?

266
00:21:38.506 --> 00:21:40.089
So. now what?

267
00:21:42.134 --> 00:21:44.760
We find an expert on
genetic mutation.

268
00:21:45.721 --> 00:21:50.016
PR ofessor of genetics.
Charles Francis Xavier.

269
00:21:52.728 --> 00:21:54.770
So. how does it feel
to be a Professor?

270
00:21:54.855 --> 00:21:56.815
Don't call me that. You don't
get to be called a Professor

271
00:21:56.898 --> 00:21:58.482
until you actually have
a teaching position.

272
00:21:58.567 --> 00:21:59.651
I know. but it suits you.

273
00:21:59.734 --> 00:22:01.403
Don't say that. Do say.
"let's go have a drink."

274
00:22:01.487 --> 00:22:03.738
Let's go have a drink.
Wonderful.

275
00:22:31.474 --> 00:22:33.143
Afternoon. gentlemen.

276
00:22:34.478 --> 00:22:35.478
Hot out there.

277
00:22:35.855 --> 00:22:37.605
Beer. please.

278
00:23:01.422 --> 00:23:03.338
German beer.
Of course.

279
00:23:04.717 --> 00:23:07.551
Yes. it's bitburger.
You like it?

280
00:23:14.018 --> 00:23:15.684
The best.

281
00:23:20.607 --> 00:23:23.401
What brings you to Argentina?

282
00:23:24.862 --> 00:23:28.198
The climate.
I'm a pig farmer.

283
00:23:32.494 --> 00:23:35.497
Tailor.
Since I was a boy.

284
00:23:35.580 --> 00:23:38.124
My father made the finest
suits in Dusseldorf.

285
00:23:39.460 --> 00:23:42.127
My parents were from Dusseldorf.

286
00:23:42.212 --> 00:23:43.337
Ah.

287
00:23:43.756 --> 00:23:44.756
What was their name?

288
00:23:45.007 --> 00:23:46.590
They didn't have a name.

289
00:23:48.594 --> 00:23:50.427
It was taken away from them...

290
00:23:50.512 --> 00:23:52.055
By pig farmers...

291
00:23:53.557 --> 00:23:54.598
And tailors.

292
00:24:23.878 --> 00:24:25.547
Blood and honor.

293
00:24:26.048 --> 00:24:27.714
Which would you
care to shed first?

294
00:24:27.842 --> 00:24:29.717
We were under orders...

295
00:24:29.884 --> 00:24:30.884
Blood then.

296
00:24:33.596 --> 00:24:34.596
Freeze. asshole.

297
00:24:35.015 --> 00:24:36.223
Come on. shoot.

298
00:24:56.912 --> 00:24:58.913
Who... what are you?

299
00:25:02.041 --> 00:25:05.169
Let's just say I'm
Frankenstein's monster.

300
00:25:16.891 --> 00:25:18.932
And I'm looking for my creator.

301
00:25:23.271 --> 00:25:25.690
Drink! Drink! Drink!

302
00:25:33.699 --> 00:25:35.657
Yeah!

303
00:25:41.414 --> 00:25:44.125
I'm so proud of you. Thank you.

304
00:25:44.209 --> 00:25:46.752
I need another drink. And
you need another cola.

305
00:25:51.090 --> 00:25:53.050
Congratulations. Professor.
Thank you very much.

306
00:25:53.134 --> 00:25:54.736
It's much harder than
it looks. actually.

307
00:25:54.802 --> 00:25:56.054
No. on your presentation.

308
00:25:56.137 --> 00:25:58.722
You were at my presentation? How
nice of you. Thank you very much.

309
00:25:58.723 --> 00:25:59.807
Moira mactaggert.

310
00:25:59.933 --> 00:26:01.893
Charles Xavier. Do
you have a minute?

311
00:26:01.977 --> 00:26:05.104
For a pretty little bean
with a mutated mcrl gene?

312
00:26:05.189 --> 00:26:06.772
I have five.

313
00:26:06.981 --> 00:26:11.653
<i>I say "MCRL." you would
say "AUBURN HAIR."</i>

314
00:26:11.778 --> 00:26:13.112
It's a mutation.

315
00:26:13.321 --> 00:26:14.864
It's a very groovy mutation.

316
00:26:15.365 --> 00:26:17.200
Mutation. right.

317
00:26:17.284 --> 00:26:21.412
took us from single-celled
organisms to the dominant form...

318
00:26:21.497 --> 00:26:24.207
You know what? This routine may
go over great with the co-eds.

319
00:26:24.290 --> 00:26:25.708
but I'm here on business.

320
00:26:25.792 --> 00:26:26.875
What?

321
00:26:27.169 --> 00:26:29.086
I really need your help.

322
00:26:29.171 --> 00:26:30.505
All right.

323
00:26:30.588 --> 00:26:34.092
The kind of mutations that you
were talking about in your thesis.

324
00:26:34.175 --> 00:26:36.176
I need to know if they may
have already happened.

325
00:26:37.805 --> 00:26:39.221
In people alive today.

326
00:26:51.192 --> 00:26:53.027
Professor?

327
00:26:54.863 --> 00:26:56.364
I think we should just
talk when you're sober.

328
00:26:56.448 --> 00:26:57.647
Do you have any time tomorrow?

329
00:26:59.451 --> 00:27:02.703
Something tells me you already
know the answer to your question.

330
00:27:05.374 --> 00:27:09.585
This is very important to me. and if
I can help you. I will do my utmost.

331
00:27:09.795 --> 00:27:10.795
Thank you.

332
00:27:14.465 --> 00:27:16.675
Still drinking champagne. Bob?

333
00:27:16.759 --> 00:27:18.720
I will pass.

334
00:27:18.804 --> 00:27:21.722
Okay. well. so much
for the pleasantries.

335
00:27:22.473 --> 00:27:25.727
I was wondering who you told
about our little arrangement.

336
00:27:25.935 --> 00:27:27.144
No one.

337
00:27:29.940 --> 00:27:32.191
- He's telling the truth.
- Good.

338
00:27:32.317 --> 00:27:34.484
Well. I guess we're done here.

339
00:27:34.569 --> 00:27:36.069
Let's wrap things up. shall we?

340
00:27:40.491 --> 00:27:42.951
Oh. I knew better
than to trust you.

341
00:27:43.912 --> 00:27:47.539
Now. you let me walk out
of here with my money.

342
00:27:47.624 --> 00:27:51.752
or I will pull this
pin. and we all die.

343
00:27:52.253 --> 00:27:55.173
Go ahead. Pull it.

344
00:27:55.257 --> 00:27:57.133
I'll do it. I swear to God.

345
00:28:06.769 --> 00:28:08.227
No. you won't.

346
00:28:12.941 --> 00:28:14.107
But I will.

347
00:28:28.039 --> 00:28:29.332
You're one of them?

348
00:28:29.415 --> 00:28:31.166
Very astute of you. colonel hendry.

349
00:28:31.542 --> 00:28:33.126
You want to guess what I can do?

350
00:28:33.295 --> 00:28:36.172
I've got the power to absorb energy.
It keeps me young.

351
00:28:36.589 --> 00:28:37.964
But that's the boring part.

352
00:28:38.258 --> 00:28:41.802
The fun stuff is what I can
do with it once I've got it.

353
00:28:48.309 --> 00:28:49.810
The advent
of the nuclear age

354
00:28:49.811 --> 00:28:51.686
may have accelerated
the mutation process.

355
00:28:52.105 --> 00:28:57.442
Individuals with extraordinary
abilities may already be among us.

356
00:28:57.528 --> 00:28:58.568
Thank you very much.

357
00:28:58.653 --> 00:29:01.239
Mactaggert. you really think
that some crackpot scientist

358
00:29:01.323 --> 00:29:05.242
is going to make me believe in
sparkly dames and vanishing men?

359
00:29:05.326 --> 00:29:08.412
You just bought yourself a one-way
ticket back to the typing pool.

360
00:29:08.497 --> 00:29:09.955
This meeting is over.

361
00:29:10.124 --> 00:29:13.459
Please sit down. agent mactaggert.

362
00:29:13.544 --> 00:29:15.502
I didn't really expect
you to believe me.

363
00:29:15.586 --> 00:29:17.755
given that all you could think
about during my presentation was

364
00:29:17.839 --> 00:29:21.217
what sort of pie they were
serving in the commissary.

365
00:29:21.300 --> 00:29:23.260
It's apple pecan.

366
00:29:23.345 --> 00:29:25.762
I haven't been entirely honest
with you. love. I'm sorry.

367
00:29:25.847 --> 00:29:28.098
You see. one of the
many spectacular things

368
00:29:28.182 --> 00:29:32.478
my mutation allows me to do
is that I can read your mind.

369
00:29:32.895 --> 00:29:35.189
I've seen this before
in a magic show.

370
00:29:35.273 --> 00:29:39.234
Are you going to ask us to think of
a number between one and 10 now?

371
00:29:39.318 --> 00:29:41.028
No. agent stryker. Although.

372
00:29:41.113 --> 00:29:43.155
I could ask you about
your son. William.

373
00:29:43.240 --> 00:29:44.865
who you were thinking
about. which is very nice.

374
00:29:44.950 --> 00:29:47.660
But I think I'd rather ask you
about the Jupiter missiles

375
00:29:47.743 --> 00:29:49.871
America are currently
placing in Turkey.

376
00:29:51.914 --> 00:29:53.082
He's a goddamn spy.

377
00:29:53.166 --> 00:29:55.835
You brought a goddamned
spy into this facility!

378
00:30:15.689 --> 00:30:17.315
How's that for a magic trick?

379
00:30:20.402 --> 00:30:22.612
Best I've ever seen.

380
00:30:23.238 --> 00:30:25.239
I want them out of here.

381
00:30:25.365 --> 00:30:28.159
And locked down until I can
figure out what to do.

382
00:30:28.993 --> 00:30:30.411
My facility is off-site.

383
00:30:32.205 --> 00:30:33.663
I'll take them.

384
00:30:34.916 --> 00:30:36.959
<i>I can't believe this. You'd
think the director of the CIA</i>

385
00:30:37.044 --> 00:30:38.169
would have a little more composure.

386
00:30:38.252 --> 00:30:39.628
We should be going
after Shaw right now.

387
00:30:39.712 --> 00:30:42.131
But instead. he's out there
worrying about the wrong mutants.

388
00:30:42.257 --> 00:30:43.758
What are we going to do. levene?

389
00:30:44.259 --> 00:30:46.801
Levene?
Levene. what's wrong with you?

390
00:30:49.347 --> 00:30:50.597
Absolutely nothing.

391
00:30:50.682 --> 00:30:53.017
I've just frozen him for a moment
because I'd like to talk to you.

392
00:30:53.101 --> 00:30:54.434
It's good. isn't it?

393
00:30:54.519 --> 00:30:57.104
I'm as interested in this
Sebastian Shaw as you are.

394
00:30:57.189 --> 00:31:01.025
If you still want my help. meet me on
the third floor of the parking garage.

395
00:31:01.317 --> 00:31:04.238
I've always known that
there were people like you out there.

396
00:31:04.320 --> 00:31:07.865
I've been the laughing stock of this
agency for years. but I knew it!

397
00:31:07.950 --> 00:31:08.907
You are going to love my facility.

398
00:31:08.991 --> 00:31:10.992
- That's going to have to wait.
- Why?

399
00:31:11.118 --> 00:31:12.953
Agent mactaggert has a
lead on Sebastian Shaw.

400
00:31:13.038 --> 00:31:15.478
and if we don't move now. apparently.
we're going to lose him.

401
00:31:15.539 --> 00:31:17.875
What?
Not only can he read minds.

402
00:31:17.960 --> 00:31:19.460
he can communicate
with them as well.

403
00:31:19.544 --> 00:31:21.461
Moira and I have just had
a lovely conversation.

404
00:31:21.462 --> 00:31:22.712
Yes. we did.

405
00:31:22.798 --> 00:31:25.048
That is incredible!

406
00:31:25.133 --> 00:31:28.134
But I cannot take you anywhere else
without permission from upstairs.

407
00:31:28.220 --> 00:31:30.221
Like to see one more
magic trick? Okay.

408
00:31:30.305 --> 00:31:32.722
Get in the car. Good idea.

409
00:31:53.287 --> 00:31:54.494
Herr doktor.

410
00:31:58.791 --> 00:32:00.875
Little Erik lensherr.

411
00:32:01.461 --> 00:32:03.086
He's here to kill you.

412
00:32:09.760 --> 00:32:12.596
What kind of a greeting is that...

413
00:32:15.057 --> 00:32:16.599
After all these years?

414
00:32:26.319 --> 00:32:28.362
Emma.

415
00:32:29.030 --> 00:32:30.614
We don't harm our own kind.

416
00:32:32.534 --> 00:32:34.785
Ah! Now it's a party.

417
00:32:36.163 --> 00:32:38.455
<i>This
is the us coast guard.</i>

418
00:32:38.539 --> 00:32:42.542
Do not attempt to move your
vessel. Stay where you are.

419
00:32:48.884 --> 00:32:50.718
They have a telepath.

420
00:32:54.221 --> 00:32:57.391
I've lost Shaw.
I've lost Shaw.

421
00:32:57.476 --> 00:32:59.309
There's something blocking me.

422
00:32:59.394 --> 00:33:00.478
This has never
happened to me before.

423
00:33:00.561 --> 00:33:02.813
I think there's someone
like me on that ship.

424
00:33:02.897 --> 00:33:05.441
Like you?
I'm sorry. a telepath.

425
00:33:05.525 --> 00:33:06.525
This is incredible.

426
00:33:06.567 --> 00:33:08.443
I could actually feel her
inside my mind. I'm very sorry.

427
00:33:08.528 --> 00:33:09.778
but I don't think I'm gonna
be much help tonight.

428
00:33:09.863 --> 00:33:10.904
You're on your own.

429
00:33:25.086 --> 00:33:26.336
Oh. my God! Jesus!

430
00:33:30.049 --> 00:33:31.634
Get inside.

431
00:33:37.098 --> 00:33:38.473
Stop. stop. stop.

432
00:33:39.934 --> 00:33:42.310
Charles!
Are you okay?

433
00:33:42.395 --> 00:33:43.635
There's someone else out there.

434
00:33:47.608 --> 00:33:48.651
There.

435
00:33:52.114 --> 00:33:53.197
Time to go.

436
00:34:48.043 --> 00:34:49.503
Let go!

437
00:34:51.630 --> 00:34:52.797
You have to let it go!

438
00:34:53.007 --> 00:34:54.800
You've got to put someone
in the water to help him.

439
00:34:54.885 --> 00:34:58.012
Let it go!
You have to let it go!

440
00:35:18.282 --> 00:35:21.784
You can't. You'll drown.
You have to let go.

441
00:35:21.869 --> 00:35:24.954
I know what this means to
you. but you're going to die.

442
00:35:25.039 --> 00:35:29.168
Please. Erik. calm your mind.

443
00:35:40.722 --> 00:35:42.306
Get off me!
Get off!

444
00:35:42.389 --> 00:35:44.641
Calm down! Just breathe.
We're here!

445
00:35:44.726 --> 00:35:46.851
Who are you?
My name is Charles Xavier.

446
00:35:47.646 --> 00:35:49.896
You were in my head.
How did you do that?

447
00:35:50.398 --> 00:35:51.981
You have your tricks.
I have mine.

448
00:35:52.067 --> 00:35:54.235
I'm like you.
Just calm your mind.

449
00:35:56.655 --> 00:35:57.905
I thought I was alone.

450
00:35:59.240 --> 00:36:00.740
You're not alone.

451
00:36:02.117 --> 00:36:04.911
Erik. you're not alone.

452
00:36:25.599 --> 00:36:28.184
Welcome to my facility.

453
00:36:28.269 --> 00:36:29.936
My mission has been to investigate

454
00:36:30.021 --> 00:36:33.106
the application of paranormal
powers in military defense.

455
00:36:33.440 --> 00:36:35.108
Or offense.

456
00:36:35.193 --> 00:36:37.402
This guy Shaw. schmidt.

457
00:36:37.487 --> 00:36:38.686
whatever you want to call him.

458
00:36:38.737 --> 00:36:40.197
he's working with the Russians.

459
00:36:40.282 --> 00:36:42.615
We might need your help to stop him.
Marvelous.

460
00:36:42.701 --> 00:36:45.661
<i>So we're to be the CIA's
new mutant division. yes?</i>

461
00:36:46.788 --> 00:36:47.954
Something like that.

462
00:36:51.418 --> 00:36:55.628
It's a supersonic.
The most advanced plane ever built.

463
00:36:57.047 --> 00:37:00.175
You should see it in real life.
It's incredible.

464
00:37:00.260 --> 00:37:04.179
Hank. these are the special new
recruits I was telling you about.

465
00:37:04.264 --> 00:37:07.224
This is Hank McCoy. one of our
most talented young researchers.

466
00:37:07.309 --> 00:37:10.978
How wonderful. Another
mutant. already here.

467
00:37:11.061 --> 00:37:13.105
Why didn't you say?

468
00:37:13.188 --> 00:37:14.315
Say what?

469
00:37:15.483 --> 00:37:17.735
Because you don't know.

470
00:37:17.818 --> 00:37:21.070
I am so. so terribly sorry.

471
00:37:23.867 --> 00:37:24.907
Hank?

472
00:37:24.992 --> 00:37:27.369
You didn't ask.
so I didn't tell.

473
00:37:27.454 --> 00:37:29.079
So. your
mutation is what?

474
00:37:29.164 --> 00:37:30.414
You're super-smart?

475
00:37:30.498 --> 00:37:31.831
I'll say.

476
00:37:31.958 --> 00:37:33.833
Hank here graduated
Harvard at the age of 15.

477
00:37:35.045 --> 00:37:37.170
I wish that's all it was.

478
00:37:37.338 --> 00:37:39.088
You're among friends now. Hank.

479
00:37:39.173 --> 00:37:40.632
You can show off.

480
00:37:56.815 --> 00:37:57.900
Splendid.

481
00:38:04.657 --> 00:38:06.199
I'm sorry.

482
00:38:12.039 --> 00:38:13.539
Ta-da!

483
00:38:20.507 --> 00:38:21.632
You're amazing.

484
00:38:22.509 --> 00:38:23.550
Really?

485
00:38:29.056 --> 00:38:30.641
<i>"The presence
of us missiles in Turkey"</i>

486
00:38:30.724 --> 00:38:32.393
<i>"represents an
unprecedented threat"</i>

487
00:38:32.476 --> 00:38:34.268
<i>"to the people of
the Soviet union."</i>

488
00:38:34.396 --> 00:38:37.731
warned Russian foreign minister
gromyko earlier today.

489
00:38:38.233 --> 00:38:41.318
But he was quick to insist the
Russians would not be the first

490
00:38:41.402 --> 00:38:43.612
to initiate any military action.

491
00:38:43.697 --> 00:38:46.489
Yeah. we'll fix that as
soon as we get to Russia.

492
00:38:46.574 --> 00:38:49.159
<i>Unless the CIA find us first.</i>

493
00:38:49.244 --> 00:38:51.411
I'll take care of them. too.

494
00:38:52.496 --> 00:38:54.914
If that telepath gets
inside your head.

495
00:38:54.998 --> 00:38:57.333
he won't be as much fun as I am.

496
00:38:57.418 --> 00:38:59.293
Already in hand. my love.

497
00:39:09.012 --> 00:39:10.931
The Russians

498
00:39:12.891 --> 00:39:15.184
made me this.

499
00:39:17.813 --> 00:39:20.440
So. what am I thinking?

500
00:39:29.826 --> 00:39:31.284
I don't know.

501
00:39:34.204 --> 00:39:36.206
I was thinking that you are
the most exquisite thing

502
00:39:36.206 --> 00:39:37.833
I have ever seen in my life.

503
00:39:42.045 --> 00:39:44.005
And that this needs ice.

504
00:39:45.507 --> 00:39:47.259
Fetch me some.

505
00:39:47.342 --> 00:39:48.635
There's a good girl.

506
00:40:13.994 --> 00:40:18.164
I promised myself I'd find a cure
ever since I was a little boy.

507
00:40:18.625 --> 00:40:22.628
You have no idea what
I'd give to feel

508
00:40:22.711 --> 00:40:24.338
normal. Normal.

509
00:40:29.052 --> 00:40:31.512
Charles has never understood.

510
00:40:31.596 --> 00:40:34.431
He's different. but
he's never had to hide.

511
00:40:35.641 --> 00:40:37.184
Hank. this serum
that you're making.

512
00:40:37.268 --> 00:40:39.769
it doesn't affect
abilities. right?

513
00:40:39.853 --> 00:40:42.773
Just appearance.
It normalizes it.

514
00:40:42.856 --> 00:40:43.981
Yeah.

515
00:40:44.775 --> 00:40:46.443
Do you think it would work on me?

516
00:40:47.987 --> 00:40:49.570
I can look into it. if you'd like.

517
00:40:49.655 --> 00:40:50.989
It's the least I can do

518
00:40:51.074 --> 00:40:53.474
after asking you to come down
here with such a weird request.

519
00:40:54.159 --> 00:40:57.286
I have to admit. usually when guys ask
me out. they're not after my blood.

520
00:40:58.081 --> 00:41:01.916
Sorry. I didn't intend
to be forward. I was just...

521
00:41:02.543 --> 00:41:06.213
I was excited. You know. the
nature of your mutation.

522
00:41:06.297 --> 00:41:09.382
If any genes hold the key to
changing appearance. it's yours.

523
00:41:09.717 --> 00:41:11.802
Hank. you weren't being forward.

524
00:41:11.885 --> 00:41:13.762
That's kind of what I meant.

525
00:41:14.639 --> 00:41:15.847
No.

526
00:41:15.931 --> 00:41:18.016
But I'm just sorry if
you thought I was.

527
00:41:18.268 --> 00:41:20.393
And I'm sorry that you weren't.

528
00:41:21.603 --> 00:41:24.063
Go ahead.
Take the blood.

529
00:41:35.827 --> 00:41:37.369
Sorry.
Did I hurt you?

530
00:41:40.164 --> 00:41:41.623
Kinky.

531
00:41:43.543 --> 00:41:47.461
By the way. if I looked like you.

532
00:41:47.588 --> 00:41:49.130
I wouldn't change a thing.

533
00:42:16.451 --> 00:42:17.490
From what
I know about you.

534
00:42:17.534 --> 00:42:19.911
I'm surprised you've
managed to stay this long.

535
00:42:21.581 --> 00:42:22.914
What do you know about me?

536
00:42:23.958 --> 00:42:25.125
Everything.

537
00:42:25.335 --> 00:42:26.918
Then you know to
stay out of my head.

538
00:42:27.378 --> 00:42:31.005
I'm sorry. Erik. but I've
seen what Shaw did to you.

539
00:42:32.592 --> 00:42:35.135
I've felt your agony.

540
00:42:36.804 --> 00:42:38.639
I can help you.

541
00:42:45.646 --> 00:42:46.813
I don't need your help.

542
00:42:46.898 --> 00:42:49.065
Don't kid yourself. You
needed my help last night.

543
00:42:49.150 --> 00:42:51.652
It's not just me you're
walking away from.

544
00:42:52.445 --> 00:42:56.572
Here you have the chance to be part of
something much bigger than yourself.

545
00:42:58.992 --> 00:43:01.786
I won't stop you leaving.
I could.

546
00:43:05.123 --> 00:43:06.625
But I won't.

547
00:43:10.545 --> 00:43:11.672
Shaw has got friends.

548
00:43:12.673 --> 00:43:14.840
You could do with some.

549
00:43:20.681 --> 00:43:23.641
<i>Hank turned that radar
installation into a transmitter.</i>

550
00:43:23.726 --> 00:43:26.268
It's designed to amplify brainwaves

551
00:43:26.353 --> 00:43:28.688
so it could enhance
your telepathic powers.

552
00:43:28.773 --> 00:43:30.898
help us find other mutants
for our division.

553
00:43:30.983 --> 00:43:33.025
What if they don't want
to be found by you?

554
00:43:33.110 --> 00:43:34.652
Erik.

555
00:43:35.028 --> 00:43:36.153
You decided to stay.

556
00:43:39.199 --> 00:43:41.367
If a new species is
being discovered.

557
00:43:41.452 --> 00:43:43.286
it should be by it's own kind.

558
00:43:43.371 --> 00:43:45.871
Charles and I find the mutants.
No suits.

559
00:43:46.123 --> 00:43:47.791
First of all. that's
my machine out there.

560
00:43:47.875 --> 00:43:50.793
Second of all. and much more
importantly. this is Charles' decision.

561
00:43:50.878 --> 00:43:52.713
<i>Charles is fine with the
CIA being involved.</i>

562
00:43:52.797 --> 00:43:54.338
Isn't that right?

563
00:43:55.800 --> 00:43:59.094
No. I'm sorry. but
I'm with Erik.

564
00:44:00.387 --> 00:44:02.304
We'll find them alone.

565
00:44:03.557 --> 00:44:04.849
What if I say no?

566
00:44:06.226 --> 00:44:09.271
Then good luck using your
installation without me.

567
00:44:21.451 --> 00:44:23.952
I call it cerebro.

568
00:44:25.246 --> 00:44:28.039
As in the Spanish for "brain." Yes.

569
00:44:28.123 --> 00:44:31.501
Okay. so. the electrodes connect Charles
to the transmitter on the roof.

570
00:44:31.585 --> 00:44:35.672
When he picks up a mutant. his brain
sends a signal through a relay

571
00:44:35.757 --> 00:44:38.842
and then the co-ordinates of their
location are printed out here.

572
00:44:38.925 --> 00:44:40.135
You designed this?

573
00:44:40.219 --> 00:44:41.302
Yeah.

574
00:44:44.766 --> 00:44:46.474
What an adorable lab
rat you make. Charles.

575
00:44:46.476 --> 00:44:48.559
Don't spoil this for me. Erik.

576
00:44:48.643 --> 00:44:51.103
I've been a lab rat. I
know one when I see one.

577
00:44:51.313 --> 00:44:55.233
Okay. great. Are you sure
we can't shave your head?

578
00:44:55.318 --> 00:44:57.443
Don't touch my hair. Okay.

579
00:45:41.072 --> 00:45:42.197
It's working!

580
00:46:00.590 --> 00:46:03.635
For that. daddy-o. you
get a private dance.

581
00:46:07.139 --> 00:46:09.099
You cats know it's
double for both. right?

582
00:46:09.182 --> 00:46:10.349
Mmm.

583
00:46:10.434 --> 00:46:12.434
No. that won't be necessary.
Although. I'm sure it'd be magical.

584
00:46:12.519 --> 00:46:15.938
We were thinking more.
we'll show you ours

585
00:46:16.023 --> 00:46:17.356
if you show us yours.

586
00:46:17.440 --> 00:46:19.818
Baby. that is not the way
it works around here.

587
00:46:21.862 --> 00:46:23.237
More tea. vicar?

588
00:46:23.614 --> 00:46:25.699
Don't mind if I do.

589
00:46:28.034 --> 00:46:29.786
My turn.

590
00:46:47.304 --> 00:46:49.972
How would you like a job where
you get to keep your clothes on?

591
00:46:55.688 --> 00:46:57.813
Where to. fellas? Richmond.
Virginia. please.

592
00:46:57.898 --> 00:47:00.817
Right. so. you want the airport?
The station? What?

593
00:47:00.902 --> 00:47:04.070
No. we were rather hoping you
would take us all the way.

594
00:47:04.322 --> 00:47:05.655
That's a six-hour drive.

595
00:47:05.739 --> 00:47:08.115
That will give us
plenty of time to talk.

596
00:47:12.079 --> 00:47:14.719
What does the government
want with a guy like Alex summers?

597
00:47:15.081 --> 00:47:16.791
I hope you're not planning
on putting him with others.

598
00:47:17.168 --> 00:47:21.670
First guy I've ever met who actually
prefers solitary confinement.

599
00:47:30.972 --> 00:47:32.431
Crazy. huh?

600
00:47:32.516 --> 00:47:33.682
What?

601
00:47:33.768 --> 00:47:35.768
You like fish. I like fish. too.

602
00:47:36.353 --> 00:47:39.688
Maybe we should get a bite
sometime. talk about it?

603
00:47:41.775 --> 00:47:43.443
I'd rather go out with the fish.

604
00:47:49.784 --> 00:47:51.534
These fish?

605
00:48:10.471 --> 00:48:12.554
Excuse me. I'm Erik lensherr.
Charles Xavier.

606
00:48:12.639 --> 00:48:14.599
Go fuck yourself.

607
00:48:34.452 --> 00:48:36.454
There's nothing on radar?
Nothing.

608
00:48:36.539 --> 00:48:38.498
Sonar?
Nyet.

609
00:48:39.416 --> 00:48:41.501
Then we have a problem.

610
00:49:00.146 --> 00:49:02.688
Beautiful. isn't it?

611
00:49:02.773 --> 00:49:04.898
The reason we exist.

612
00:49:04.983 --> 00:49:07.110
We are the children
of the atom. my love.

613
00:49:07.445 --> 00:49:08.610
We have a situation.

614
00:49:09.530 --> 00:49:10.905
The telepath.

615
00:49:10.989 --> 00:49:13.199
I shouldn't be able to
feel him at this distance.

616
00:49:13.367 --> 00:49:15.659
It's like his reach is

617
00:49:15.744 --> 00:49:16.869
amplified.

618
00:49:20.206 --> 00:49:22.291
They're recruiting.

619
00:49:22.376 --> 00:49:26.045
You go on to Russia.
I'll handle them.

620
00:49:27.715 --> 00:49:29.996
I can't stop thinking
about the others out there.

621
00:49:30.050 --> 00:49:33.887
All those minds that I touched.
I could feel them.

622
00:49:34.804 --> 00:49:39.309
Their isolation. their
hopes. their ambitions.

623
00:49:39.393 --> 00:49:41.853
I tell you. we are at the start
of something incredible. Erik.

624
00:49:41.853 --> 00:49:43.063
We can help them.

625
00:49:43.563 --> 00:49:44.813
Can we?

626
00:49:46.108 --> 00:49:49.277
Identification.
that's how it starts.

627
00:49:50.570 --> 00:49:54.114
And ends with being rounded up.
experimented on. eliminated.

628
00:49:54.199 --> 00:49:55.992
Not this time.

629
00:49:56.077 --> 00:49:58.327
We have common enemies.
Shaw. the Russians.

630
00:49:58.411 --> 00:49:59.954
They need us.

631
00:50:00.039 --> 00:50:01.498
For now.

632
00:50:07.128 --> 00:50:08.568
We should
think of code names.

633
00:50:08.755 --> 00:50:11.195
We're government agents now. we
should have secret code names.

634
00:50:11.300 --> 00:50:12.460
I want to be called mystique.

635
00:50:12.802 --> 00:50:15.344
Damn! I wanted to
be called mystique.

636
00:50:15.429 --> 00:50:17.347
Well. tough. I called it.

637
00:50:18.932 --> 00:50:21.643
And I'm way more
mysterious than you.

638
00:50:24.188 --> 00:50:25.438
Darwin. what about you?

639
00:50:25.773 --> 00:50:27.731
Well. "Darwin" is
already a nickname.

640
00:50:27.817 --> 00:50:30.360
and. you know. it sort of fits.

641
00:50:30.443 --> 00:50:31.820
Adapt to survive and all.

642
00:50:32.445 --> 00:50:34.489
Check this out.

643
00:50:42.164 --> 00:50:43.331
Whoa!

644
00:50:47.503 --> 00:50:49.253
That was incredible. Thank you.

645
00:50:49.797 --> 00:50:51.005
What about you?

646
00:50:51.090 --> 00:50:53.757
I'm going to be.

647
00:50:53.842 --> 00:50:54.884
Banshee.

648
00:50:54.969 --> 00:50:56.760
Why do you want to be named
after a wailing spirit?

649
00:50:56.846 --> 00:50:58.206
You might want to cover your ears.

650
00:51:14.487 --> 00:51:15.822
Your turn.

651
00:51:15.905 --> 00:51:17.824
My stage name is angel.

652
00:51:19.159 --> 00:51:21.286
It kind of fits. You can fly?

653
00:51:21.744 --> 00:51:23.163
Uh-huh. And...

654
00:51:32.338 --> 00:51:33.338
What's your name?

655
00:51:34.675 --> 00:51:35.800
How about big foot?

656
00:51:36.510 --> 00:51:39.262
You know what they say
about guys with big feet.

657
00:51:39.346 --> 00:51:41.306
And yours are kind of small.

658
00:51:41.389 --> 00:51:42.681
Okay. now.

659
00:51:44.059 --> 00:51:45.934
Alex. what is your gift?
What can you do?

660
00:51:46.103 --> 00:51:48.771
It's not...

661
00:51:48.856 --> 00:51:51.065
I just can't do it. I
can't do it in here.

662
00:51:51.192 --> 00:51:53.443
Why
don't you just do it out there?

663
00:51:53.527 --> 00:51:57.155
Alex!
Alex! Alex!

664
00:52:02.036 --> 00:52:03.536
That's the spirit!

665
00:52:03.621 --> 00:52:05.704
Get down when I tell you.

666
00:52:05.789 --> 00:52:07.623
<i>"Get down
when I tell you."</i>

667
00:52:12.545 --> 00:52:13.630
Get back.

668
00:52:19.177 --> 00:52:20.219
Get back!

669
00:52:21.847 --> 00:52:23.514
Whatever.

670
00:52:37.112 --> 00:52:41.282
We have intel that Shaw is meeting with
the Russian defense chief in moscow.

671
00:52:41.367 --> 00:52:43.492
So go ahead. Say it.

672
00:52:43.577 --> 00:52:45.994
I'm not here to say "I told you
so." You know why I'm here.

673
00:52:46.079 --> 00:52:48.748
Yeah. yeah. yeah. Clearance
to bring along your mutants.

674
00:52:48.831 --> 00:52:52.293
Fight fire with fire.
It makes sense.

675
00:52:52.378 --> 00:52:54.253
Wait! You're okay with this?

676
00:52:54.338 --> 00:52:57.130
Sending in a bunch of
untrained. unauthorized freaks?

677
00:52:57.215 --> 00:53:01.677
These freaks are dedicated.
hardworking people.

678
00:53:02.762 --> 00:53:04.264
Plane leaves for Russia in an hour.

679
00:53:04.347 --> 00:53:06.349
I'm telling you. these kids
are not ready for Shaw.

680
00:53:06.349 --> 00:53:07.391
I think they're gonna surprise you.

681
00:53:07.476 --> 00:53:08.726
They're an exceptional
bunch of young people.

682
00:53:08.811 --> 00:53:09.851
What the hell?

683
00:53:18.820 --> 00:53:20.862
Come on! You can
go harder than that.

684
00:53:22.699 --> 00:53:25.617
Harder!

685
00:53:28.621 --> 00:53:30.289
What are you doing?

686
00:53:36.297 --> 00:53:37.838
Who destroyed the statue?

687
00:53:37.922 --> 00:53:39.423
It was Alex.

688
00:53:39.507 --> 00:53:40.800
No. havok.

689
00:53:40.884 --> 00:53:42.969
We have to call him havok.
That's his name now.

690
00:53:43.052 --> 00:53:46.806
And we were thinking. you
should be Professor x

691
00:53:46.974 --> 00:53:49.057
and you should be Magneto.

692
00:53:50.476 --> 00:53:51.601
Exceptional.

693
00:53:56.317 --> 00:53:57.858
I expect more from you.

694
00:54:19.005 --> 00:54:20.380
We got a problem. What?

695
00:54:20.465 --> 00:54:22.550
I'm so sorry. This
wasn't on the map.

696
00:54:29.141 --> 00:54:30.474
No matter what
happens. act normally.

697
00:54:30.559 --> 00:54:32.393
I'll take care of this. all right?

698
00:54:33.686 --> 00:54:34.728
Now. listen to me...

699
00:54:37.900 --> 00:54:40.318
- Where are you going?
- To our farm.

700
00:54:42.570 --> 00:54:43.945
Open the back.

701
00:54:44.030 --> 00:54:45.947
As you wish.

702
00:54:50.244 --> 00:54:52.121
Easy. easy.
Take it easy. chaps.

703
00:55:08.097 --> 00:55:10.597
- Anything back there?
- Nothing. It's empty.

704
00:55:13.893 --> 00:55:15.561
- Everything okay?
- Yes.

705
00:55:38.751 --> 00:55:41.336
- Where is Shaw?
- I don't know.

706
00:55:41.422 --> 00:55:44.757
But if she's a telepath and I
read her. she'll know we're here.

707
00:55:46.092 --> 00:55:48.094
Let me try something else.

708
00:56:05.362 --> 00:56:07.780
Shaw sends his apologies
but he's indisposed.

709
00:56:07.864 --> 00:56:10.490
He asked me to come in his place.

710
00:56:10.576 --> 00:56:14.786
And between you and I. honey.
I'm a lot better company.

711
00:56:14.871 --> 00:56:15.996
Please. come in.

712
00:56:21.461 --> 00:56:22.461
He's not coming.

713
00:56:25.298 --> 00:56:27.215
So. what now. boss?

714
00:56:27.300 --> 00:56:29.802
Now. nothing. We're here
for Shaw. Mission aborted.

715
00:56:29.887 --> 00:56:31.637
The hell it is. Erik.

716
00:56:31.722 --> 00:56:34.389
She's his right-hand woman.
That's good enough for me.

717
00:56:34.682 --> 00:56:38.143
<i>The CIA invading the home of a senior
Soviet official. Are you crazy?</i>

718
00:56:38.769 --> 00:56:40.313
<i>I'm not CIA.</i>

719
00:56:40.606 --> 00:56:41.606
Erik!

720
00:56:44.818 --> 00:56:46.318
Your health.

721
00:56:50.657 --> 00:56:52.574
So. you must be busy
planning your next move.

722
00:56:52.659 --> 00:56:55.869
What with the Americans refusing to
remove their missiles from Turkey.

723
00:56:57.331 --> 00:57:00.500
You know I can't talk about
those things. miss frost.

724
00:57:01.126 --> 00:57:02.585
Emma.

725
00:57:05.463 --> 00:57:07.507
And don't worry.

726
00:57:08.050 --> 00:57:10.175
You don't have to say a word.

727
00:57:26.025 --> 00:57:27.400
He's gonna start
world war III single-handed.

728
00:57:27.485 --> 00:57:30.070
We have to do something.
Like what?

729
00:57:30.155 --> 00:57:31.489
We're moving out.
You can't!

730
00:57:47.755 --> 00:57:49.590
I'm sorry.
I can't leave him.

731
00:58:01.728 --> 00:58:03.521
For God's sake. Erik!
Be calm.

732
00:58:04.898 --> 00:58:06.231
Be calm.

733
00:58:06.775 --> 00:58:08.483
Forget my face.

734
00:58:17.577 --> 00:58:22.039
You are beautiful. so beautiful!
Yes!

735
00:58:22.541 --> 00:58:24.291
Pathetic.

736
00:58:32.342 --> 00:58:33.759
Yes!

737
00:58:35.887 --> 00:58:36.929
Nice trick.

738
00:58:39.724 --> 00:58:40.724
Who are you?

739
00:58:44.771 --> 00:58:45.771
Go to sleep.

740
00:58:54.197 --> 00:58:56.197
You can stop trying to
read my mind. sugar.

741
00:58:58.619 --> 00:59:01.119
You're never going to get anything
from me while I'm like this.

742
00:59:14.259 --> 00:59:15.498
So. then. you can just tell us.

743
00:59:18.554 --> 00:59:19.972
Where is Shaw?

744
00:59:26.271 --> 00:59:27.438
Erik.

745
00:59:33.987 --> 00:59:35.153
Erik. that's enough.

746
00:59:43.829 --> 00:59:44.871
Erik. that's enough!

747
00:59:55.092 --> 00:59:56.092
All yours.

748
00:59:57.719 --> 01:00:00.596
She won't be shifting
into diamond form again.

749
01:00:00.681 --> 01:00:03.056
And if she does. just
give her a gentle tap.

750
01:00:29.166 --> 01:00:32.378
We are the
children of the atom.

751
01:00:32.461 --> 01:00:35.380
Radiation gave birth to mutants.

752
01:00:35.465 --> 01:00:39.844
What will kill the humans
will only make us stronger.

753
01:00:44.224 --> 01:00:45.266
Beautiful. isn't it?

754
01:00:48.686 --> 01:00:51.230
This is worse than we
previously imagined.

755
01:00:53.608 --> 01:00:55.358
We're taking you with us.

756
01:00:55.443 --> 01:00:57.527
<i>CIA will want to
question you themselves.</i>

757
01:00:57.612 --> 01:00:59.320
Oh. I doubt it.

758
01:00:59.405 --> 01:01:02.490
They have bigger things
to worry about right now.

759
01:01:08.081 --> 01:01:10.331
- Whoa!
- All right. all right.

760
01:01:10.416 --> 01:01:12.376
Jesus. man. you are killing me.

761
01:01:12.460 --> 01:01:15.588
Don't beat yourself up. I've
had a lot of spare time.

762
01:01:20.427 --> 01:01:22.219
Oh. I didn't know the
circus was in town.

763
01:01:22.637 --> 01:01:25.237
Hey. come on. honey. Give us a little...

764
01:01:25.556 --> 01:01:28.016
No?
Come on. let's see the foot.

765
01:01:28.101 --> 01:01:29.726
There it is. Come on.
big foot. let's go.

766
01:01:29.811 --> 01:01:32.146
Hey. Hey. come on. Hey.

767
01:01:36.485 --> 01:01:38.527
They're just guys being stupid.

768
01:01:38.612 --> 01:01:40.237
Guys being stupid. I can handle.

769
01:01:40.322 --> 01:01:41.905
Okay?
I've handled that my whole life.

770
01:01:42.282 --> 01:01:44.407
But I'd rather a bunch of guys
stare at me with my clothes off

771
01:01:44.492 --> 01:01:45.893
than the way these
ones stare at me.

772
01:01:47.788 --> 01:01:48.788
At us.

773
01:01:57.130 --> 01:01:58.130
What was that?

774
01:02:00.592 --> 01:02:02.885
I don't know.
Something doesn't feel right.

775
01:02:11.894 --> 01:02:13.103
No news of Shaw?

776
01:02:13.646 --> 01:02:16.481
Not a peep. Not even
through that back channel?

777
01:02:28.994 --> 01:02:30.036
What is that?

778
01:02:47.514 --> 01:02:49.034
We have an intruder
in the main atrium.

779
01:02:49.099 --> 01:02:50.306
Where are the mutants?

780
01:02:50.391 --> 01:02:52.141
If you take another step.
I'm gonna put you down.

781
01:02:52.226 --> 01:02:55.521
Of course you will. But where do
I find the more evolved people?

782
01:02:56.398 --> 01:02:57.690
Send back-up now!

783
01:03:00.860 --> 01:03:03.778
Get back! Do not leave that
room. We're under attack!

784
01:03:05.030 --> 01:03:06.030
Shoot! Shoot!

785
01:03:19.713 --> 01:03:20.753
Where are the mutants?

786
01:03:20.838 --> 01:03:23.298
Put that man down
or we will open fire!

787
01:03:48.992 --> 01:03:50.951
Stay here. my ass! Let's go!

788
01:03:56.666 --> 01:03:59.208
Get back! We can help!
We can help!

789
01:04:58.936 --> 01:04:59.936
Wait!

790
01:04:59.980 --> 01:05:01.813
You want the mutants? They're
right through that door.

791
01:05:01.981 --> 01:05:04.273
Just let us normal people go.
We're no threat...

792
01:05:14.494 --> 01:05:16.829
- Where is the telepath?
- Not here.

793
01:05:17.288 --> 01:05:18.664
Too bad.

794
01:05:18.873 --> 01:05:20.713
Well. at least I can take
this silly thing off.

795
01:05:23.003 --> 01:05:26.838
Good evening.
My name is Sebastian Shaw.

796
01:05:28.173 --> 01:05:30.217
And I am not here to hurt you.

797
01:05:30.510 --> 01:05:31.802
Freeze!

798
01:05:32.177 --> 01:05:33.762
Azazel.

799
01:05:37.099 --> 01:05:40.643
My friends. there is
a revolution coming.

800
01:05:40.728 --> 01:05:44.106
When mankind discovers who
we are. what we can do.

801
01:05:44.190 --> 01:05:45.940
each of us will face a choice.

802
01:05:46.775 --> 01:05:48.193
Be enslaved

803
01:05:49.528 --> 01:05:51.237
or rise up to rule.

804
01:05:52.282 --> 01:05:54.449
Choose freely. but know that
if you are not with us.

805
01:05:54.534 --> 01:05:56.284
then. by definition. you are

806
01:05:56.661 --> 01:05:58.202
against us.

807
01:05:59.039 --> 01:06:01.206
So. you can stay

808
01:06:01.833 --> 01:06:04.793
and fight for the people
who hate and fear you.

809
01:06:16.264 --> 01:06:17.556
and queens.

810
01:06:29.235 --> 01:06:30.818
Angel. Are you kidding me?

811
01:06:31.695 --> 01:06:33.489
Come on.

812
01:06:33.572 --> 01:06:35.407
We don't belong here.

813
01:06:35.824 --> 01:06:37.909
And that's nothing
to be ashamed of.

814
01:06:42.916 --> 01:06:44.875
We have to do something.

815
01:07:00.141 --> 01:07:02.976
Stop.
I'm coming with you.

816
01:07:06.940 --> 01:07:08.606
Good choice.

817
01:07:09.608 --> 01:07:11.652
So. tell me about your mutation.

818
01:07:12.528 --> 01:07:14.112
Well. I adapt to survive.

819
01:07:17.784 --> 01:07:19.242
So. I guess I'm coming with you.

820
01:07:19.911 --> 01:07:21.452
I like that.

821
01:07:27.710 --> 01:07:29.128
Alex! Get out!

822
01:07:29.253 --> 01:07:30.628
Do it!

823
01:07:35.467 --> 01:07:37.552
Protecting your fellow mutants?

824
01:07:38.471 --> 01:07:39.887
That's a noble gesture.

825
01:07:40.514 --> 01:07:42.056
Feels good.

826
01:07:47.813 --> 01:07:49.481
Adapt to this.

827
01:08:33.650 --> 01:08:35.402
Hello.

828
01:08:36.654 --> 01:08:43.618
<i>Once again. my sympathies for your
treatment at the hands of the CIA.</i>

829
01:08:43.869 --> 01:08:46.872
These Americans are ruthless.

830
01:08:48.041 --> 01:08:52.543
Now they have their missiles
placed in Turkey...

831
01:08:53.587 --> 01:08:57.841
I expect you'll be planning new
missile sites of your own.

832
01:08:58.176 --> 01:09:04.555
Somewhere you know the American
early-warning system won't help.

833
01:09:05.182 --> 01:09:09.185
I hear Cuba is lovely
this time of year.

834
01:09:09.895 --> 01:09:12.396
And so close to Florida.

835
01:09:13.733 --> 01:09:15.734
Missiles in Cuba?

836
01:09:17.987 --> 01:09:19.695
You're serious?

837
01:09:20.405 --> 01:09:23.283
We may as well declare war.

838
01:09:24.368 --> 01:09:26.411
Maybe I wasn't clear enough.

839
01:09:28.957 --> 01:09:31.291
You will make this happen.

840
01:09:33.127 --> 01:09:34.418
Okay.

841
01:09:35.087 --> 01:09:37.506
Let's see
what kgb think about this.

842
01:09:42.177 --> 01:09:45.596
Hello?
General armivolkoff.

843
01:09:48.475 --> 01:09:51.270
It's nothing.

844
01:10:06.411 --> 01:10:07.828
Raven?

845
01:10:13.710 --> 01:10:15.711
We've made arrangements for you
to be taken home immediately.

846
01:10:15.795 --> 01:10:17.296
We're not going home.
What?

847
01:10:17.838 --> 01:10:19.715
He's not going back to prison.

848
01:10:19.798 --> 01:10:20.923
He killed Darwin.

849
01:10:21.009 --> 01:10:22.448
All the more reason
for you to leave.

850
01:10:22.844 --> 01:10:24.261
This is over.

851
01:10:24.345 --> 01:10:26.387
Darwin's dead. Charles.

852
01:10:26.471 --> 01:10:28.306
And we can't even bury him.

853
01:10:31.144 --> 01:10:32.226
We can avenge him.

854
01:10:35.773 --> 01:10:37.774
Erik. a word. please.

855
01:10:41.154 --> 01:10:42.194
They're just kids.

856
01:10:42.279 --> 01:10:44.405
No. They were kids.

857
01:10:44.489 --> 01:10:46.824
Shaw has his army. we need ours.

858
01:10:52.707 --> 01:10:53.998
We'll have to train.

859
01:10:54.833 --> 01:10:56.710
All of us.

860
01:10:56.793 --> 01:10:58.420
Yes? Yeah.

861
01:10:59.296 --> 01:11:01.088
Well. we can't stay here.

862
01:11:01.173 --> 01:11:04.509
Even if they reopen the
department. it's not safe.

863
01:11:04.594 --> 01:11:06.677
We've got nowhere to go.

864
01:11:09.349 --> 01:11:10.431
Yes. we do.

865
01:11:11.391 --> 01:11:13.393
The law says we've
got to turn her over.

866
01:11:13.478 --> 01:11:15.604
The law applies
to human beings.

867
01:11:15.688 --> 01:11:19.106
The same laws don't apply to
mutants. They're too dangerous.

868
01:11:19.192 --> 01:11:23.362
In times like this. security is
more important than liberty.

869
01:11:23.445 --> 01:11:24.820
There is a war coming. John.

870
01:11:24.905 --> 01:11:26.073
Yes.

871
01:11:26.698 --> 01:11:28.283
but a war with who?

872
01:11:42.381 --> 01:11:44.466
Excellent question.

873
01:11:44.550 --> 01:11:47.301
Though I wouldn't call
it a war. exactly.

874
01:11:47.386 --> 01:11:50.764
That suggests both sides stand
an equal chance of winning.

875
01:12:00.274 --> 01:12:02.818
Captain. no sign of
any American ships.

876
01:12:03.110 --> 01:12:05.654
Maintain course. full ahead.

877
01:12:06.238 --> 01:12:09.157
The Russians have
sent their warheads to Cuba.

878
01:12:09.242 --> 01:12:11.368
We have a week before the
ship hits the coast.

879
01:12:11.452 --> 01:12:15.579
Our fleet can be on this line when
the Russian missile ship arrives.

880
01:12:16.332 --> 01:12:19.167
If that ship crosses the line.

881
01:12:19.252 --> 01:12:22.337
they will have declared war
against the United States.

882
01:12:22.421 --> 01:12:25.966
And we will have no choice but to
retaliate with a full nuclear response.

883
01:12:26.050 --> 01:12:27.091
Do we agree?

884
01:12:32.597 --> 01:12:35.266
Dispatch the 7th fleet.

885
01:12:37.353 --> 01:12:38.854
This is yours?

886
01:12:38.938 --> 01:12:41.148
No. it's ours.

887
01:12:47.320 --> 01:12:52.074
Honestly. Charles. I don't know how you
survived. living in such hardship.

888
01:12:52.201 --> 01:12:55.744
Well. it was a hardship
softened by me.

889
01:12:58.332 --> 01:13:00.292
Come on. Time for the tour.

890
01:13:13.221 --> 01:13:15.181
Dear comrades...

891
01:13:15.307 --> 01:13:21.979
The United States have
dispatched warships for Cuba.

892
01:13:23.064 --> 01:13:26.984
This leaves us with no choice.

893
01:13:28.404 --> 01:13:31.823
Comrade first secretary...

894
01:13:32.658 --> 01:13:35.327
We must send in our fleet.

895
01:13:38.497 --> 01:13:39.997
Dispatch the fleet!

896
01:13:46.005 --> 01:13:48.923
President Kennedy
has signed a formal proclamation

897
01:13:49.007 --> 01:13:52.551
setting up a blockade of all
missiles bound for Cuba.

898
01:13:53.762 --> 01:13:55.889
The Soviet
union reacted by terming it.

899
01:13:55.890 --> 01:13:59.850
"A step along the road to
unleashing a thermo-nuclear war."

900
01:14:10.695 --> 01:14:11.738
You're sure?

901
01:14:12.280 --> 01:14:13.989
I'm sure.

902
01:14:14.074 --> 01:14:15.617
All right.

903
01:14:22.207 --> 01:14:24.208
No. No. I can't. I'm sorry.

904
01:14:24.292 --> 01:14:26.461
I can't shoot anybody point
blank. let alone my friend.

905
01:14:26.546 --> 01:14:28.546
Oh. come on. You know
I can deflect it.

906
01:14:28.631 --> 01:14:29.965
You're always telling me
I should push myself.

907
01:14:30.048 --> 01:14:31.423
If you know you can deflect it.

908
01:14:31.509 --> 01:14:35.261
then you're not
challenging yourself.

909
01:14:35.345 --> 01:14:38.640
Whatever happened to the man who
was trying to raise a submarine?

910
01:14:38.724 --> 01:14:41.434
I can't. Something that big?

911
01:14:41.519 --> 01:14:43.144
I need the situation. the anger...

912
01:14:43.229 --> 01:14:44.854
No. the anger is not enough.

913
01:14:45.730 --> 01:14:47.274
It's gotten the job
done all this time.

914
01:14:47.567 --> 01:14:49.442
It's nearly gotten you
killed all this time.

915
01:14:50.653 --> 01:14:52.570
Come here.

916
01:14:52.654 --> 01:14:54.573
Let's try something a
little more challenging.

917
01:14:56.283 --> 01:15:00.578
My stepfather took the possibility of
nuclear war quite seriously. This way.

918
01:15:00.662 --> 01:15:02.788
That is why he had this
bunker built down here.

919
01:15:02.872 --> 01:15:05.332
I thought we could use it as
a practice range of sorts.

920
01:15:05.417 --> 01:15:07.335
You don't think I'm going
to blow through the walls?

921
01:15:07.420 --> 01:15:09.628
He had this place built
to withstand a nuclear bomb.

922
01:15:09.713 --> 01:15:11.088
I think it can handle you. Alex.

923
01:15:11.756 --> 01:15:14.426
You know. when I do this.
bad things tend to happen.

924
01:15:14.510 --> 01:15:18.596
That's because you can't
control it. It controls you.

925
01:15:18.680 --> 01:15:21.099
That's why we're here. Alex.
It's why we're training.

926
01:15:26.271 --> 01:15:27.551
What you're doing is incredible.

927
01:15:27.606 --> 01:15:28.856
You're hitting a pitch
with sound waves

928
01:15:28.940 --> 01:15:31.568
that have the same resonant frequency
as the glass. That's why it shatters.

929
01:15:31.652 --> 01:15:34.154
But this. it's like any
other muscle in the body.

930
01:15:34.238 --> 01:15:36.197
You can control it.

931
01:15:37.658 --> 01:15:40.368
"In each of us. two
natures are at war."

932
01:15:40.453 --> 01:15:42.203
Robert Louis Stevenson.
Jekyll and Hyde.

933
01:15:42.287 --> 01:15:43.329
Top marks.

934
01:15:43.413 --> 01:15:45.372
The story wasn't really about
good and evil though. was it?

935
01:15:45.457 --> 01:15:47.250
It was about man's animal nature

936
01:15:47.335 --> 01:15:49.336
and his struggle to
control it. to conform.

937
01:15:49.920 --> 01:15:51.962
And it's that struggle
which is holding you back.

938
01:15:52.297 --> 01:15:55.300
No. Jekyll was afraid of
what he could be capable of.

939
01:15:55.384 --> 01:15:57.135
And you are. too.

940
01:15:57.219 --> 01:15:59.511
If you're serious about me doing
this. you might want to get back.

941
01:15:59.680 --> 01:16:01.014
All right.

942
01:16:01.265 --> 01:16:03.099
Shall I shut the door? Yeah.

943
01:16:06.228 --> 01:16:08.479
Whenever you're ready.

944
01:16:14.944 --> 01:16:15.987
Oh. my God!

945
01:16:19.617 --> 01:16:21.909
I will teach you to
control this. Alex.

946
01:16:25.372 --> 01:16:27.457
And you're sure that
this will work?

947
01:16:27.541 --> 01:16:29.333
Anything is possible.
I based the design...

948
01:16:29.417 --> 01:16:31.752
Hank. stop talking. Come on.

949
01:16:32.128 --> 01:16:33.921
Now. remember. Scream
as hard as you can.

950
01:16:34.006 --> 01:16:35.881
You need the sound waves
to be supersonic.

951
01:16:36.007 --> 01:16:38.208
Catch them at the right angle
and they should carry you.

952
01:16:38.344 --> 01:16:40.470
They should carry me.

953
01:16:40.554 --> 01:16:43.139
That's reassuring. Good luck.

954
01:16:44.140 --> 01:16:45.975
And don't forget to scream.

955
01:16:55.194 --> 01:16:56.944
Now. if you want to
beat me this time.

956
01:16:57.029 --> 01:16:59.363
you have to set the beast free.

957
01:17:00.240 --> 01:17:01.699
On your marks.

958
01:17:02.158 --> 01:17:03.283
get set.

959
01:17:03.703 --> 01:17:05.036
go!

960
01:17:19.426 --> 01:17:21.469
Congratulations. my friend.

961
01:17:21.554 --> 01:17:23.314
<i>Robert Louis Stevenson
would have been proud.</i>

962
01:17:25.224 --> 01:17:26.765
Impressive. Hank.

963
01:17:26.850 --> 01:17:28.770
With feet like those. all
you need is a red nose.

964
01:17:28.978 --> 01:17:30.603
Right. bozo?

965
01:17:30.688 --> 01:17:32.730
I'm done here. Thank you. Alex.

966
01:17:33.983 --> 01:17:35.190
Come on. Hank.

967
01:17:45.911 --> 01:17:48.662
If you're using half your
concentration to look normal.

968
01:17:49.247 --> 01:17:52.375
then you're only half paying attention
to whatever else you're doing.

969
01:17:52.752 --> 01:17:56.087
Just pointing out something
that could save your life.

970
01:17:59.591 --> 01:18:01.259
You want society to accept you.

971
01:18:02.344 --> 01:18:05.012
but you can't even accept yourself.

972
01:18:10.644 --> 01:18:12.436
Sexy!

973
01:18:12.520 --> 01:18:13.979
Well. this is just the prototype.

974
01:18:14.064 --> 01:18:15.523
The real one will look
considerably better.

975
01:18:15.608 --> 01:18:18.568
It will be a whole suit. See. these
sensors measure your energy output.

976
01:18:18.652 --> 01:18:21.362
This panel focuses it and
the excess is absorbed.

977
01:18:21.654 --> 01:18:22.863
Try hitting the one in the middle.

978
01:18:22.948 --> 01:18:24.269
Just the one in the middle. mind.

979
01:18:24.949 --> 01:18:26.117
Good luck.

980
01:18:36.252 --> 01:18:39.087
You got to see this. Your genes
are extraordinary. you know that?

981
01:18:39.172 --> 01:18:40.840
Your cells age at half the
rate of a normal human.

982
01:18:40.925 --> 01:18:43.717
When you're 40. you'll still have
the leucocytes of a teenager.

983
01:18:43.802 --> 01:18:48.222
You have the most incredible
cellular structure I've ever seen.

984
01:18:52.603 --> 01:18:54.436
And you truly
believe I'll fly this time?

985
01:18:54.521 --> 01:18:55.854
Unreservedly.

986
01:18:56.314 --> 01:18:57.606
I trust you. I'm touched.

987
01:18:57.690 --> 01:18:59.484
I don't trust him.
Say nothing.

988
01:19:00.694 --> 01:19:02.237
I'm gonna die!

989
01:19:02.320 --> 01:19:04.238
Look. we're not going to make you
do anything you don't feel...

990
01:19:04.323 --> 01:19:05.573
Here. let me help.

991
01:19:07.408 --> 01:19:08.451
Erik!

992
01:19:29.681 --> 01:19:31.181
What?

993
01:19:31.266 --> 01:19:32.934
You know you were
thinking the same.

994
01:19:33.685 --> 01:19:35.103
Wonderful work. Hank.
Thank you very much.

995
01:19:35.186 --> 01:19:36.979
All right. Alex. I want
you to hit the "X".

996
01:19:37.856 --> 01:19:39.537
And try not to hit me.
There's a good chap.

997
01:19:40.484 --> 01:19:43.027
You're serious?
I'm very serious.

998
01:19:43.529 --> 01:19:45.363
I have complete and
utter faith in you.

999
01:19:58.668 --> 01:19:59.711
Am I still a bozo?

1000
01:20:00.378 --> 01:20:03.171
Yes. Hank. you're still a bozo.

1001
01:20:03.423 --> 01:20:04.423
But nice job.

1002
01:20:07.677 --> 01:20:08.802
See that?

1003
01:20:09.512 --> 01:20:11.639
Try turning it to face us.

1004
01:20:30.533 --> 01:20:35.662
You know. I believe that true focus lies
somewhere between rage and serenity.

1005
01:20:37.582 --> 01:20:39.333
Would you mind if I...

1006
01:21:13.786 --> 01:21:15.411
What did you just do to me?

1007
01:21:16.788 --> 01:21:20.582
I accessed the brightest
corner of your memory system.

1008
01:21:22.377 --> 01:21:25.546
It's a very beautiful
memory. Erik. Thank you.

1009
01:21:25.631 --> 01:21:28.256
I didn't know I still had that.

1010
01:21:28.884 --> 01:21:31.551
There is so much more
to you than you know.

1011
01:21:31.636 --> 01:21:34.639
Not just pain and anger.

1012
01:21:34.722 --> 01:21:36.306
There is good. too.
I felt it.

1013
01:21:37.643 --> 01:21:39.560
When you can access all of that.

1014
01:21:40.061 --> 01:21:42.814
you'll possess a power
no one can match.

1015
01:21:43.981 --> 01:21:45.399
Not even me.

1016
01:21:47.069 --> 01:21:49.654
So. come on. Try again.

1017
01:22:30.194 --> 01:22:31.738
Hey! Well done.

1018
01:22:32.029 --> 01:22:33.864
The president is about
to make his address.

1019
01:22:35.868 --> 01:22:39.953
It shall be the policy of
this nation to regard any nuclear missile

1020
01:22:40.037 --> 01:22:43.666
crossing the embargo
line that surrounds Cuba

1021
01:22:43.751 --> 01:22:47.962
as an attack by the Soviet
union on the United States

1022
01:22:48.046 --> 01:22:51.716
requiring a full retaliatory
response upon the Soviet union...

1023
01:22:51.800 --> 01:22:52.966
That's where we're
going to find Shaw.

1024
01:22:53.051 --> 01:22:54.176
How do you know?

1025
01:22:54.261 --> 01:22:57.971
Two superpowers facing off and
he wants to start world war III.

1026
01:22:58.055 --> 01:22:59.724
He won't leave anything to chance.

1027
01:22:59.891 --> 01:23:01.725
So much for diplomacy.

1028
01:23:01.810 --> 01:23:04.186
I suggest you all get
a good night's sleep.

1029
01:23:04.270 --> 01:23:06.314
Ultimately
leads to war.

1030
01:23:07.274 --> 01:23:11.652
Tensions mount as the
Soviet missile ship nears Cuba.

1031
01:23:11.737 --> 01:23:16.532
All diplomatic efforts to avert
nuclear war have thus far failed.

1032
01:23:16.617 --> 01:23:18.493
As the American people
ready themselves

1033
01:23:18.577 --> 01:23:20.994
for the likelihood
of an atomic attack.

1034
01:23:21.078 --> 01:23:24.498
there are widespread
reports of panic-buying.

1035
01:23:24.582 --> 01:23:28.920
supermarkets cleared. as shelters
unused since the second world war

1036
01:23:29.003 --> 01:23:31.506
are stocked for what may lie ahead.

1037
01:23:31.590 --> 01:23:36.176
In all it's history. America has
never faced a greater threat.

1038
01:23:36.345 --> 01:23:38.054
The world is primed for war

1039
01:23:38.221 --> 01:23:40.640
and there's no one to stop me.

1040
01:23:45.645 --> 01:23:46.686
Come in.

1041
01:23:47.814 --> 01:23:49.231
Hey.

1042
01:23:49.942 --> 01:23:51.943
I have a surprise for you.

1043
01:24:00.409 --> 01:24:03.996
I isolated the right
marker in your DNA sample.

1044
01:24:04.081 --> 01:24:05.872
The serum works like an antibiotic.

1045
01:24:05.957 --> 01:24:09.126
attacking the cells that
'cause our physical mutation.

1046
01:24:09.211 --> 01:24:11.962
It won't affect our abilities.
just our appearance.

1047
01:24:14.632 --> 01:24:16.259
Do you still want to do this?

1048
01:24:17.719 --> 01:24:19.804
Should we have to hide?

1049
01:24:21.180 --> 01:24:23.056
Well. you already do.

1050
01:24:23.140 --> 01:24:26.060
You're hiding right now.
like I have my whole life.

1051
01:24:26.854 --> 01:24:30.146
I don't want to feel like a freak all
the time. I just want to look...

1052
01:24:30.231 --> 01:24:32.315
Normal. Yeah.

1053
01:24:39.615 --> 01:24:40.658
Hank. don't!

1054
01:24:42.911 --> 01:24:44.996
You're beautiful. Hank.

1055
01:24:45.079 --> 01:24:47.331
Everything you are.
you are perfect.

1056
01:24:49.917 --> 01:24:53.253
Look at all of us. Look at all
we've achieved this week.

1057
01:24:53.337 --> 01:24:55.338
All we will achieve.

1058
01:24:56.507 --> 01:24:58.967
We are different.

1059
01:24:59.051 --> 01:25:01.470
But we shouldn't be trying
to fit into society.

1060
01:25:02.555 --> 01:25:05.725
Society should aspire
to be more like us.

1061
01:25:06.726 --> 01:25:09.770
Mutant and proud.

1062
01:25:14.859 --> 01:25:16.569
It behooves me to tell you

1063
01:25:16.653 --> 01:25:18.738
that even if we save
the world tomorrow.

1064
01:25:18.822 --> 01:25:21.948
and mutants are
accepted into society.

1065
01:25:22.033 --> 01:25:25.453
my feet and your natural blue form

1066
01:25:25.537 --> 01:25:27.454
will never be deemed beautiful.

1067
01:25:32.920 --> 01:25:34.377
You look beautiful now.

1068
01:25:36.506 --> 01:25:39.591
We need this cure.

1069
01:26:06.619 --> 01:26:08.662
Cuba.

1070
01:26:08.747 --> 01:26:10.288
Russia. America.

1071
01:26:10.373 --> 01:26:12.332
It makes no difference.

1072
01:26:12.417 --> 01:26:15.377
Shaw has declared war on
mankind. on all of us.

1073
01:26:15.462 --> 01:26:16.462
He has to be stopped.

1074
01:26:18.340 --> 01:26:19.590
I'm not going to stop Shaw.

1075
01:26:20.550 --> 01:26:21.591
I'm going to kill him.

1076
01:26:24.762 --> 01:26:27.305
Do you have it in
you to allow that?

1077
01:26:33.063 --> 01:26:35.439
You've known all along
why I was here. Charles.

1078
01:26:35.856 --> 01:26:38.149
But things have changed.

1079
01:26:38.234 --> 01:26:40.194
What started as a covert mission.

1080
01:26:40.278 --> 01:26:43.029
tomorrow. mankind will
know that mutants exist.

1081
01:26:43.114 --> 01:26:46.199
Shaw. us. they won't differentiate.

1082
01:26:46.283 --> 01:26:47.868
They'll fear us.

1083
01:26:48.119 --> 01:26:49.828
And that fear will turn to hatred.

1084
01:26:50.162 --> 01:26:51.997
Not if we stop a war.

1085
01:26:52.082 --> 01:26:53.373
Not if we can prevent Shaw.

1086
01:26:53.457 --> 01:26:55.376
Not if we risk our lives doing so.

1087
01:26:55.502 --> 01:26:56.702
Would they do the same for us?

1088
01:26:56.752 --> 01:26:58.628
We have it in us to
be the better men.

1089
01:26:58.713 --> 01:27:00.672
We already are.

1090
01:27:00.756 --> 01:27:02.382
We're the next stage
of human evolution.

1091
01:27:02.466 --> 01:27:04.510
You said it yourself! No...

1092
01:27:04.594 --> 01:27:06.386
Are you really so naive

1093
01:27:06.470 --> 01:27:09.806
as to think that they won't
battle their own extinction?

1094
01:27:10.559 --> 01:27:12.018
Or is it arrogance?

1095
01:27:12.101 --> 01:27:13.476
I'm sorry?

1096
01:27:14.061 --> 01:27:15.938
After tomorrow. they're
going to turn on us.

1097
01:27:16.023 --> 01:27:19.274
But you're blind to it. because you
believe they're all like moira.

1098
01:27:19.693 --> 01:27:21.652
And you believe they're
all like Shaw.

1099
01:27:24.197 --> 01:27:28.242
Listen to me very
carefully. my friend.

1100
01:27:28.326 --> 01:27:31.244
Killing Shaw will not
bring you peace.

1101
01:27:32.997 --> 01:27:35.541
Peace was never an option.

1102
01:28:21.755 --> 01:28:23.005
No.

1103
01:28:24.466 --> 01:28:25.882
No. no. No.

1104
01:28:54.912 --> 01:28:56.704
Well.

1105
01:28:58.332 --> 01:28:59.792
this is a surprise.

1106
01:29:00.085 --> 01:29:01.543
The nice kind?

1107
01:29:03.462 --> 01:29:07.006
Get out. raven. I
want to go to bed.

1108
01:29:07.091 --> 01:29:09.551
Maybe in a few years.

1109
01:29:13.515 --> 01:29:15.140
How about now?

1110
01:29:20.063 --> 01:29:21.604
I prefer the real raven.

1111
01:29:25.569 --> 01:29:28.988
I said the real raven.

1112
01:29:37.956 --> 01:29:39.247
Perfection.

1113
01:29:43.878 --> 01:29:45.378
Could you pass me my robe?

1114
01:29:45.671 --> 01:29:47.881
You don't have to hide.

1115
01:29:51.970 --> 01:29:53.636
Have you ever looked at a tiger

1116
01:29:53.846 --> 01:29:56.640
and thought you ought
to cover it up?

1117
01:29:58.018 --> 01:29:59.518
No. but...

1118
01:29:59.728 --> 01:30:02.061
You're an exquisite
creature. raven.

1119
01:30:03.606 --> 01:30:06.108
All your life. the world
has tried to tame you.

1120
01:30:06.943 --> 01:30:08.569
It's time for you to be free.

1121
01:30:29.381 --> 01:30:31.550
You know. sometimes I wonder
what my life would have been like

1122
01:30:31.635 --> 01:30:33.927
if you hadn't found
me here that night.

1123
01:30:34.011 --> 01:30:35.470
Sorry. what? You...

1124
01:30:37.681 --> 01:30:39.515
For God's sake. raven!

1125
01:30:39.600 --> 01:30:41.851
Where are your clothes?
Put some clothes on.

1126
01:30:41.936 --> 01:30:43.811
That's not what you said
when you first saw me.

1127
01:30:44.605 --> 01:30:48.149
But I guess pets are always cuter
when they're little. right?

1128
01:30:48.234 --> 01:30:50.194
Raven. I don't know what's
gotten into you lately.

1129
01:30:50.612 --> 01:30:52.070
I thought you'd be in a good mood.

1130
01:30:52.613 --> 01:30:58.077
Hank. he tells me that he's found the
answer to your cosmetic problem.

1131
01:30:59.537 --> 01:31:00.703
Are you gonna tell
me what's the matter

1132
01:31:00.788 --> 01:31:02.029
or do I have to read your mind?

1133
01:31:02.498 --> 01:31:04.166
You promised me you
would never do that.

1134
01:31:04.251 --> 01:31:05.917
Until recently.

1135
01:31:06.002 --> 01:31:08.837
I never had to use my power to know
what you were thinking. raven.

1136
01:31:08.921 --> 01:31:12.757
Charles. I used to think it was going
to be you and me against the world.

1137
01:31:12.841 --> 01:31:14.385
But no matter how
bad the world gets.

1138
01:31:14.469 --> 01:31:16.177
you don't want to be
against it. do you?

1139
01:31:16.262 --> 01:31:17.384
You want to be a part of it.

1140
01:31:39.911 --> 01:31:41.078
What the hell happened here?

1141
01:31:49.587 --> 01:31:51.380
Hank has been busy.

1142
01:31:51.463 --> 01:31:53.631
Do we really have to wear these?

1143
01:31:53.716 --> 01:31:56.467
As none of us mutated to
endure extreme g-force

1144
01:31:56.552 --> 01:31:59.805
or being riddled by bullets.
I suggest we suit up.

1145
01:32:24.288 --> 01:32:25.622
Where is Hank?

1146
01:32:27.458 --> 01:32:28.958
I'm here.

1147
01:32:38.427 --> 01:32:40.220
Hank?

1148
01:32:45.310 --> 01:32:48.479
It didn't attack the cells.

1149
01:32:48.563 --> 01:32:52.024
It enhanced them.

1150
01:32:52.108 --> 01:32:53.399
It didn't work.

1151
01:32:53.859 --> 01:32:56.653
Yes. it did. Hank.
Don't you see?

1152
01:32:56.988 --> 01:33:00.157
This is who you were meant to be.

1153
01:33:00.533 --> 01:33:01.867
This is you.

1154
01:33:04.037 --> 01:33:05.371
No more hiding.

1155
01:33:06.331 --> 01:33:08.664
You never looked better. man.
Hank!

1156
01:33:10.502 --> 01:33:12.795
Don't mock me!

1157
01:33:12.878 --> 01:33:14.759
Hank. put him
down immediately. please.

1158
01:33:14.881 --> 01:33:15.922
Hank! Hank!

1159
01:33:18.926 --> 01:33:20.344
I wasn't.

1160
01:33:20.761 --> 01:33:22.470
Even I got to admit you
look pretty badass.

1161
01:33:23.014 --> 01:33:24.472
I think I got a new name for you.

1162
01:33:25.350 --> 01:33:26.432
Beast.

1163
01:33:28.936 --> 01:33:30.520
You're sure you can fly this thing?

1164
01:33:30.688 --> 01:33:33.356
Of course I can. I designed it.

1165
01:33:45.369 --> 01:33:47.162
Status of
the cargo ship.

1166
01:33:47.247 --> 01:33:50.791
Bearing
1-8-0 at 12 knots.

1167
01:33:52.585 --> 01:33:54.877
Three minutes to the
embargo line. sir.

1168
01:33:56.046 --> 01:33:58.798
God help them if they cross it.

1169
01:34:00.510 --> 01:34:01.717
God help us all.

1170
01:34:02.429 --> 01:34:03.804
Sound general quarters.

1171
01:34:03.887 --> 01:34:05.471
General quarters. general quarters!

1172
01:34:06.640 --> 01:34:08.560
- All hands. man battle stations!
- Aye. sir.

1173
01:34:08.643 --> 01:34:10.226
Set condition zebra!

1174
01:34:10.895 --> 01:34:12.938
General
quarters. battle stations.

1175
01:34:24.117 --> 01:34:29.078
Captain. we already have our
orders. Why so eager for new ones?

1176
01:34:29.538 --> 01:34:33.041
I lived through one war. comrade.

1177
01:34:34.377 --> 01:34:36.587
I'd prefer not to start another.

1178
01:34:38.965 --> 01:34:41.175
Battle stations! Now!

1179
01:34:43.845 --> 01:34:48.765
Gun boss. target cargo
ship bearing 1-8-0.

1180
01:34:50.810 --> 01:34:53.645
Fleet reports all weapons ready.

1181
01:34:54.104 --> 01:34:55.939
From the kremlin. sir.

1182
01:34:56.483 --> 01:35:00.444
New orders. As of 1025 hours. the cargo
vessel aral sea is hereby ordered to...

1183
01:35:00.819 --> 01:35:03.113
Reverse course and return
to port in Odessa.

1184
01:35:03.280 --> 01:35:07.283
Aral sea. come in.

1185
01:35:08.453 --> 01:35:09.869
They are not responding.

1186
01:35:09.953 --> 01:35:11.121
She's not turning around.

1187
01:35:11.372 --> 01:35:13.957
Aral sea. you are
ordered to turn around.

1188
01:35:14.292 --> 01:35:15.626
Do not cross the line.

1189
01:35:16.793 --> 01:35:18.753
Target ready to be fired upon. sir.

1190
01:35:18.837 --> 01:35:21.797
Stand by to fire. Standing by. sir.

1191
01:35:29.431 --> 01:35:30.849
Whoa!

1192
01:35:34.311 --> 01:35:36.896
It looks pretty messy out there.

1193
01:35:47.158 --> 01:35:49.618
Aral sea you are ordered
to turn around.

1194
01:35:50.537 --> 01:35:53.247
The crew of the aral sea are
all dead. Shaw's been there.

1195
01:35:53.331 --> 01:35:54.831
He's still here. somewhere.

1196
01:35:54.916 --> 01:35:56.792
He set the ship on course
for the embargo line.

1197
01:35:56.876 --> 01:35:58.085
If that ship crosses the line.

1198
01:35:58.168 --> 01:35:59.752
our boys are going to blow it up.

1199
01:35:59.837 --> 01:36:01.505
And the war begins.

1200
01:36:01.922 --> 01:36:03.422
Unless they're not our boys.

1201
01:36:06.426 --> 01:36:08.970
USS independence. this
is Alexander nevsky.

1202
01:36:09.055 --> 01:36:10.846
We have lost control
of our cargo ship.

1203
01:36:10.931 --> 01:36:12.599
She has been instructed to stop.

1204
01:36:12.684 --> 01:36:15.560
Do not fire! Repeat.
do not fire!

1205
01:36:15.645 --> 01:36:19.021
They have signaled the cargo
ship to turn around. sir.

1206
01:36:19.106 --> 01:36:21.483
It's a ruse. Pay no attention!

1207
01:36:21.859 --> 01:36:24.444
Stand by to fire.
Standing by to fire. sir.

1208
01:36:24.529 --> 01:36:26.697
On my count. Five.

1209
01:36:27.198 --> 01:36:28.573
four...

1210
01:36:50.887 --> 01:36:52.346
Hold on!

1211
01:37:01.733 --> 01:37:02.858
Nyet.

1212
01:37:07.195 --> 01:37:09.155
What was that? The Russians.

1213
01:37:09.239 --> 01:37:10.657
They have fired on
their own ship.

1214
01:37:11.408 --> 01:37:12.908
A little warning next
time. Professor.

1215
01:37:13.286 --> 01:37:16.203
Sorry about that. You all right?
Yeah.

1216
01:37:16.913 --> 01:37:18.414
Son of a...

1217
01:37:18.498 --> 01:37:21.001
Give me cinclant on the horn.
I want a new set of orders.

1218
01:37:25.006 --> 01:37:27.090
Congratulations. comrade.

1219
01:37:27.425 --> 01:37:31.261
You just averted nuclear war!

1220
01:37:31.845 --> 01:37:33.220
What?

1221
01:37:33.305 --> 01:37:34.972
Take him to the brig.

1222
01:37:35.057 --> 01:37:38.726
What?
What just happened?

1223
01:37:38.810 --> 01:37:40.770
They say the comrade lost his mind.

1224
01:37:40.979 --> 01:37:43.606
The Americans are applauding.

1225
01:37:44.609 --> 01:37:48.153
They're here. That
telepath is powerful.

1226
01:37:50.323 --> 01:37:53.033
We're moving to a back-up plan.

1227
01:37:54.827 --> 01:37:56.243
That was inspired. Charles.

1228
01:37:56.328 --> 01:37:58.372
Thank you very much. but I
still can't locate Shaw.

1229
01:37:58.456 --> 01:38:00.498
He's down there. We
need to find him now.

1230
01:38:00.582 --> 01:38:01.582
Hank?

1231
01:38:01.667 --> 01:38:04.002
Is there anything unusual
on the radar or scanners?

1232
01:38:04.087 --> 01:38:05.670
No. Nothing.

1233
01:38:06.797 --> 01:38:08.381
Well. then he must be underwater.

1234
01:38:08.466 --> 01:38:10.050
And obviously. we don't have sonar.

1235
01:38:12.595 --> 01:38:15.180
Yes. we do. Yes. we do.

1236
01:38:19.976 --> 01:38:21.136
They are ready for war.

1237
01:38:21.354 --> 01:38:23.979
We just need to strike another
match to light the fuse.

1238
01:38:24.314 --> 01:38:27.149
And we still have the most
powerful weapon of all.

1239
01:38:27.902 --> 01:38:28.944
Me.

1240
01:38:29.278 --> 01:38:34.157
Turn the nuclear reactor to 100% output
and make sure I'm not disturbed.

1241
01:38:37.537 --> 01:38:39.578
Hank. level the bloody plane!

1242
01:38:44.752 --> 01:38:47.002
Whoa! You back right off.

1243
01:38:48.213 --> 01:38:50.006
Beast. open the bomb bay doors!

1244
01:38:58.349 --> 01:39:01.309
Remember! This is a muscle.

1245
01:39:01.394 --> 01:39:03.019
You control it!

1246
01:39:03.104 --> 01:39:05.439
You'll be in here
the entire time!

1247
01:39:05.689 --> 01:39:07.189
We'll see you soon!

1248
01:39:07.274 --> 01:39:10.777
On my mark! Three! Two!

1249
01:39:11.279 --> 01:39:12.863
One! Go!

1250
01:39:29.546 --> 01:39:31.797
Alert the fleet. they may
want to take their cans off.

1251
01:39:45.061 --> 01:39:47.605
Banshee has got a
location on Shaw.

1252
01:39:49.609 --> 01:39:50.942
Are you ready for this?

1253
01:39:51.027 --> 01:39:52.319
Let's find out.

1254
01:40:56.091 --> 01:40:58.885
Remember. the
point between rage

1255
01:40:59.177 --> 01:41:01.304
and serenity.

1256
01:42:24.555 --> 01:42:25.721
Erik. take my hand!

1257
01:42:26.390 --> 01:42:27.515
Oh.

1258
01:42:27.600 --> 01:42:30.268
Hold on. guys. It's
gonna get bumpy.

1259
01:42:45.743 --> 01:42:47.077
Erik. take my hand!

1260
01:43:38.421 --> 01:43:40.046
Moira? Moira. are you all right?

1261
01:43:40.131 --> 01:43:41.922
Yeah. I'm okay.

1262
01:43:46.052 --> 01:43:47.804
I read the teleporter's mind.

1263
01:43:47.887 --> 01:43:49.805
Shaw is drawing all the
power out of his sub.

1264
01:43:49.890 --> 01:43:51.975
He's turning himself into
some kind of nuclear bomb.

1265
01:43:52.100 --> 01:43:54.341
We got no time. The geiger
count is going out of control.

1266
01:43:54.395 --> 01:43:55.520
Moira. this is what
we're gonna do.

1267
01:43:55.604 --> 01:43:58.314
Get on the radio and tell them to
clear both fleets out immediately.

1268
01:43:58.314 --> 01:44:00.692
I'm going in. Beast.
havok. back him up.

1269
01:44:00.775 --> 01:44:02.735
Erik. I can guide you
through once you're in.

1270
01:44:02.819 --> 01:44:05.279
but I need you to shut down
whatever it is that's blocking me.

1271
01:44:05.363 --> 01:44:07.407
then we just hope to God it's not
too late for me to stop him.

1272
01:44:07.490 --> 01:44:09.492
Got it. Good luck!

1273
01:44:09.577 --> 01:44:11.286
Raven. stop! I'm
going to help them.

1274
01:44:11.369 --> 01:44:12.494
We don't have time for this.

1275
01:44:12.496 --> 01:44:13.579
If anything comes in that entrance.

1276
01:44:13.663 --> 01:44:15.289
you're taking care of it. yes?

1277
01:44:15.373 --> 01:44:16.498
Fine.

1278
01:44:33.100 --> 01:44:34.184
Beast!

1279
01:44:37.729 --> 01:44:39.439
If we go. you go!

1280
01:44:42.984 --> 01:44:45.194
We believe Shaw is trying to
detonate some kind of bomb.

1281
01:44:50.451 --> 01:44:52.911
Erik. make for the
middle of the vessel.

1282
01:44:52.994 --> 01:44:54.595
That's the point my
mind can't penetrate.

1283
01:44:54.662 --> 01:44:56.872
We have to assume that
that's where Shaw is.

1284
01:45:05.716 --> 01:45:07.675
Gangway! Gangway! Gangway!

1285
01:45:14.682 --> 01:45:17.435
That's the nuclear reactor.
Disable it.

1286
01:45:29.907 --> 01:45:31.908
Stop! Don't move!

1287
01:45:39.667 --> 01:45:40.917
Get down!

1288
01:46:04.399 --> 01:46:05.942
Erik. you're there.
You've reached the void.

1289
01:46:06.025 --> 01:46:08.610
He's not here. Charles. Shaw's
not here! He's left the sub!

1290
01:46:08.820 --> 01:46:10.697
What? He's got to be there.
He has to be!

1291
01:46:10.780 --> 01:46:12.573
There's nowhere else he can be.
Keep looking.

1292
01:46:12.574 --> 01:46:16.202
And I'm telling you he's not.
There's no one here. God damn it!

1293
01:46:19.247 --> 01:46:20.957
Erik.

1294
01:46:21.417 --> 01:46:22.876
What a pleasant surprise.

1295
01:46:22.960 --> 01:46:24.460
Erik? Erik.

1296
01:46:27.171 --> 01:46:28.922
So good to see you again.

1297
01:46:45.649 --> 01:46:48.859
May I ask you something?

1298
01:46:48.944 --> 01:46:50.612
Why are you on their side?

1299
01:46:50.695 --> 01:46:51.820
He's gone. What?

1300
01:46:51.905 --> 01:46:54.782
He's gone into the void! I can't
communicate with him there.

1301
01:46:54.867 --> 01:46:57.452
Why fight for a doomed
race who will hunt us down

1302
01:46:57.536 --> 01:47:00.496
as soon as they realize their
reign is coming to an end?

1303
01:47:29.318 --> 01:47:31.444
Yeah! Yes!

1304
01:47:44.457 --> 01:47:46.376
I'm sorry for what
happened in the camps.

1305
01:47:48.628 --> 01:47:50.462
I truly am.

1306
01:47:58.721 --> 01:48:01.975
He's back! Erik. whatever
you're doing. keep doing it.

1307
01:48:02.059 --> 01:48:04.060
It's starting to work.

1308
01:48:04.185 --> 01:48:07.063
But everything I
did. I did for you.

1309
01:48:07.564 --> 01:48:09.231
To unlock your power.

1310
01:48:09.399 --> 01:48:11.734
to make you embrace it.

1311
01:48:15.072 --> 01:48:16.197
It's working!

1312
01:48:16.280 --> 01:48:18.699
I'm starting to see him. but
I can't yet touch his mind.

1313
01:48:33.090 --> 01:48:35.841
You've come a long way
from bending gates.

1314
01:48:35.926 --> 01:48:37.635
I'm so proud of you.

1315
01:48:45.601 --> 01:48:48.061
And you're just starting
to scratch the surface.

1316
01:48:48.439 --> 01:48:51.481
Think how much further we could go

1317
01:48:51.567 --> 01:48:53.525
together.

1318
01:49:04.121 --> 01:49:05.203
Look out!

1319
01:49:12.462 --> 01:49:14.463
Stop! Azazel.

1320
01:49:29.729 --> 01:49:32.439
I don't want to hurt you. Erik.
I never did.

1321
01:49:32.524 --> 01:49:34.149
I want to help you.

1322
01:49:34.359 --> 01:49:36.485
This is our time.

1323
01:49:36.612 --> 01:49:38.320
Our age.

1324
01:49:38.988 --> 01:49:43.201
We are the future
of the human race.

1325
01:49:43.284 --> 01:49:45.787
You and me. son.

1326
01:49:45.871 --> 01:49:48.372
This world could be ours.

1327
01:49:49.917 --> 01:49:53.877
Everything you did
made me stronger.

1328
01:49:54.796 --> 01:49:57.506
It made me the weapon I am today.

1329
01:49:59.009 --> 01:50:01.010
It's the truth.

1330
01:50:01.929 --> 01:50:04.305
I've known it all along.

1331
01:50:09.978 --> 01:50:11.938
You are my creator.

1332
01:50:12.689 --> 01:50:14.189
Now. Charles!

1333
01:50:15.734 --> 01:50:17.609
Are you okay? Moira. be quiet.

1334
01:50:17.694 --> 01:50:19.487
I can only control
this man for so long.

1335
01:50:33.210 --> 01:50:34.918
- Sorry. Charles.
- Erik. please.

1336
01:50:35.212 --> 01:50:36.295
Be the better man.

1337
01:50:36.380 --> 01:50:37.630
It's not that I don't trust you.

1338
01:50:37.631 --> 01:50:39.422
Erik. there will be
no turning back!

1339
01:50:40.884 --> 01:50:42.301
No!

1340
01:50:43.052 --> 01:50:44.886
Charles!
Don't do this. Erik!

1341
01:50:52.229 --> 01:50:53.729
If you're in there.

1342
01:50:53.855 --> 01:50:56.899
I'd like you to know that I
agree with every word you said.

1343
01:50:59.569 --> 01:51:01.570
We are the future.

1344
01:51:03.448 --> 01:51:04.489
But.

1345
01:51:06.534 --> 01:51:07.868
unfortunately.

1346
01:51:08.662 --> 01:51:11.079
you killed my mother.

1347
01:51:19.213 --> 01:51:20.672
This is what we're going to do.

1348
01:51:20.756 --> 01:51:23.091
No. Please. Erik. no.

1349
01:51:23.176 --> 01:51:27.054
I'm going to count to three and
I'm going to move the coin.

1350
01:51:29.099 --> 01:51:30.765
One.

1351
01:51:31.976 --> 01:51:33.769
Please. Erik.

1352
01:51:41.819 --> 01:51:43.445
Two.

1353
01:51:49.953 --> 01:51:51.662
Three.

1354
01:52:20.067 --> 01:52:22.902
The Russians
share our concerns

1355
01:52:22.985 --> 01:52:25.988
and will join a strike
on all the mutants.

1356
01:52:26.073 --> 01:52:28.073
We can end this threat for good.

1357
01:52:28.158 --> 01:52:30.076
We'll never have another
opportunity like this.

1358
01:52:30.159 --> 01:52:32.078
We have an agent on that beach.

1359
01:52:32.162 --> 01:52:34.037
One agent.

1360
01:52:34.163 --> 01:52:35.497
She's a good agent.

1361
01:52:35.582 --> 01:52:37.792
She's collateral damage.

1362
01:52:43.297 --> 01:52:46.676
Today. our fighting stops!

1363
01:53:09.824 --> 01:53:12.284
Take off your blinders.
brothers and sisters.

1364
01:53:13.036 --> 01:53:14.787
The real enemy is out there.

1365
01:53:16.747 --> 01:53:18.791
I feel their guns
moving in the water.

1366
01:53:19.251 --> 01:53:21.543
their metal targeting us.

1367
01:53:21.752 --> 01:53:24.130
Americans. Soviets.

1368
01:53:24.297 --> 01:53:25.881
humans.

1369
01:53:26.507 --> 01:53:29.051
United in their fear
of the unknown.

1370
01:53:30.220 --> 01:53:33.972
The neanderthal is running
scared. my fellow mutants!

1371
01:53:36.225 --> 01:53:37.310
Go ahead. Charles.

1372
01:53:39.895 --> 01:53:41.063
Tell me I'm wrong.

1373
01:54:01.501 --> 01:54:04.337
Fleet commander. this
is X-ray bravo 7-0.

1374
01:54:04.421 --> 01:54:06.838
Respond. Over.

1375
01:54:06.922 --> 01:54:09.257
The beach is secure.
Call off the attack.

1376
01:54:09.551 --> 01:54:11.969
The beach is targeted and
ready to be fired upon. sir.

1377
01:54:12.054 --> 01:54:14.346
Stand by. Standing by. sir.

1378
01:54:14.555 --> 01:54:16.306
New orders. Fire on the beach.

1379
01:54:18.476 --> 01:54:20.060
Hello?

1380
01:54:21.604 --> 01:54:23.564
Hello!

1381
01:54:30.363 --> 01:54:33.114
Fire!

1382
01:55:21.706 --> 01:55:24.166
Erik. you said yourself.
we're the better men.

1383
01:55:24.835 --> 01:55:26.418
This is the time to prove it.

1384
01:55:30.172 --> 01:55:32.257
There are thousands of
men on those ships.

1385
01:55:32.341 --> 01:55:34.592
Good. honest. innocent men!

1386
01:55:34.677 --> 01:55:36.470
They're just following orders.

1387
01:55:38.390 --> 01:55:40.640
I've been at the mercy of
men just following orders.

1388
01:55:45.689 --> 01:55:47.189
Never again.

1389
01:55:51.485 --> 01:55:52.903
Erik. release them!

1390
01:55:59.743 --> 01:56:01.537
No!

1391
01:56:07.586 --> 01:56:10.045
I don't want to hurt you.
Don't make me!

1392
01:56:10.881 --> 01:56:11.963
Stand back!

1393
01:56:14.717 --> 01:56:16.010
Charles. that's enough!

1394
01:56:21.056 --> 01:56:22.182
Erik. stop!

1395
01:56:32.569 --> 01:56:34.778
Gentlemen. it's been an
honor serving with you.

1396
01:56:34.988 --> 01:56:37.489
Comrades. thank you
for your service.

1397
01:57:24.996 --> 01:57:26.287
I'm so sorry.

1398
01:57:26.372 --> 01:57:28.414
I said back off!

1399
01:57:29.917 --> 01:57:32.211
You. You did this.

1400
01:57:36.216 --> 01:57:38.716
Erik. Please.

1401
01:57:40.886 --> 01:57:43.889
She didn't do this. Erik.

1402
01:57:43.974 --> 01:57:45.975
You did.

1403
01:57:52.481 --> 01:57:56.150
Us turning on each other.
it's what they want.

1404
01:57:56.653 --> 01:57:59.488
I tried to warn you. Charles.

1405
01:58:01.283 --> 01:58:03.742
I want you by my side.

1406
01:58:03.827 --> 01:58:05.786
We're brothers. you and I.

1407
01:58:06.078 --> 01:58:09.289
All of us together.
protecting each other.

1408
01:58:11.208 --> 01:58:13.543
We want the same thing.

1409
01:58:14.128 --> 01:58:16.046
My friend.

1410
01:58:16.506 --> 01:58:20.341
I'm sorry. but we do not.

1411
01:58:36.109 --> 01:58:39.903
Charles! I'm sorry.
I'm so sorry.

1412
01:58:39.988 --> 01:58:42.488
It's all right.
It's all right.

1413
01:58:46.036 --> 01:58:48.369
This society won't accept us.

1414
01:58:49.456 --> 01:58:50.956
We form our own.

1415
01:58:51.373 --> 01:58:54.208
The humans have played their hand.

1416
01:58:55.878 --> 01:58:58.421
Now we get ready to play ours.

1417
01:59:00.884 --> 01:59:01.966
Who's with me?

1418
01:59:13.604 --> 01:59:15.021
No more hiding.

1419
01:59:43.009 --> 01:59:44.301
You should go with him.

1420
01:59:44.969 --> 01:59:46.345
It's what you want.

1421
01:59:46.887 --> 01:59:49.264
You promised me you would
never read my mind.

1422
01:59:49.682 --> 01:59:51.100
I know.

1423
01:59:51.184 --> 01:59:53.435
I promised you a great
many things. I'm afraid.

1424
01:59:54.520 --> 01:59:55.645
I'm sorry.

1425
02:00:00.984 --> 02:00:03.112
Take care of him.

1426
02:00:17.918 --> 02:00:21.003
And. beast. never forget.

1427
02:00:21.715 --> 02:00:25.007
Mutant and proud.

1428
02:00:33.393 --> 02:00:35.185
Help
me out. come on.

1429
02:00:35.686 --> 02:00:37.520
I'm gonna get you to a hospital.

1430
02:00:37.604 --> 02:00:39.314
Wait. Charles.

1431
02:00:39.399 --> 02:00:41.065
Charles. don't move. okay?

1432
02:00:41.150 --> 02:00:42.943
I won't.

1433
02:00:43.027 --> 02:00:44.862
Actually...

1434
02:00:48.158 --> 02:00:50.242
I can't feel my legs.

1435
02:00:51.202 --> 02:00:53.578
What? I can't feel my legs.

1436
02:00:55.164 --> 02:00:57.166
I can't feel my legs.

1437
02:01:08.845 --> 02:01:10.595
In this
week of Thanksgiving

1438
02:01:10.680 --> 02:01:12.639
there is much for which
we can be grateful

1439
02:01:12.724 --> 02:01:16.185
as we look back to where we
stood only four weeks ago.

1440
02:01:16.269 --> 02:01:19.688
The unity of this hemisphere.
the support of our allies

1441
02:01:19.773 --> 02:01:22.608
and the calm determination
of the American people.

1442
02:01:22.692 --> 02:01:26.444
These qualities may be tested
many more times in this decade.

1443
02:01:29.698 --> 02:01:32.408
So. how many students
do you think you'll have here

1444
02:01:32.493 --> 02:01:34.787
once you get the academy
up and running?

1445
02:01:34.871 --> 02:01:37.038
As many as I can manage.

1446
02:01:37.122 --> 02:01:38.957
Possibly more.

1447
02:01:41.543 --> 02:01:42.627
You know.

1448
02:01:43.546 --> 02:01:45.380
one day the government
is going to realize

1449
02:01:45.465 --> 02:01:47.882
how lucky they were to have
Professor x on their side.

1450
02:01:49.676 --> 02:01:52.136
I suppose I am a real
Professor now. aren't I?

1451
02:01:52.221 --> 02:01:53.783
Next thing you know.
I'll be going bald.

1452
02:01:55.475 --> 02:01:57.935
We're still on the
government's side. moira.

1453
02:01:58.353 --> 02:02:00.561
We're still g-men.
Just without the "g".

1454
02:02:01.355 --> 02:02:04.774
No. You're your own team now.

1455
02:02:04.943 --> 02:02:06.400
It's better.

1456
02:02:07.194 --> 02:02:09.404
You're X-Men.

1457
02:02:11.114 --> 02:02:13.158
Yes. I like the sound of that.

1458
02:02:14.077 --> 02:02:15.368
Moira?

1459
02:02:15.869 --> 02:02:19.747
For us. anonymity will be
the first line of defense.

1460
02:02:20.542 --> 02:02:22.000
I know.

1461
02:02:23.086 --> 02:02:27.631
They can threaten me all
they want. Charles.

1462
02:02:27.715 --> 02:02:30.551
I'll never tell them where you are.

1463
02:02:30.635 --> 02:02:32.511
Ever.

1464
02:02:32.595 --> 02:02:34.555
I know you won't.

1465
02:02:35.931 --> 02:02:37.349
I know.

1466
02:02:44.815 --> 02:02:47.650
I remember the attack on hq.

1467
02:02:47.734 --> 02:02:50.028
leaving to go somewhere else.

1468
02:02:50.113 --> 02:02:54.157
And then this morning.
I woke up at home.

1469
02:02:54.242 --> 02:02:56.368
That's it.

1470
02:02:56.452 --> 02:02:59.954
All that time. wiped clean
from your mind. Just gone.

1471
02:03:00.622 --> 02:03:02.457
He can do that? You don't
remember anything?

1472
02:03:03.208 --> 02:03:05.460
Sometimes I get fragments.

1473
02:03:05.627 --> 02:03:07.421
Like

1474
02:03:07.505 --> 02:03:09.547
trees.

1475
02:03:09.631 --> 02:03:11.091
sunlight.

1476
02:03:12.969 --> 02:03:14.011
A kiss.

1477
02:03:14.095 --> 02:03:16.220
Oh. Jesus.

1478
02:03:16.305 --> 02:03:19.557
<i>Gentlemen. this is why the
CIA is no place for a woman.</i>

1479
02:03:24.439 --> 02:03:25.564
What the hell was that?

1480
02:03:42.497 --> 02:03:45.207
I know we've had our differences.

1481
02:03:47.587 --> 02:03:49.755
Where's your telepath friend?

1482
02:03:50.381 --> 02:03:52.506
Gone.

1483
02:03:52.591 --> 02:03:55.510
Left a bit of a gap in my
life. if I'm to be honest.

1484
02:03:55.595 --> 02:03:58.387
I was rather hoping
you would fill it.

1485
02:04:02.685 --> 02:04:03.935
Join us.

1486
02:04:11.402 --> 02:04:12.735
Erik. I believe.

1487
02:04:16.698 --> 02:04:18.367
I prefer

1488
02:04:20.203 --> 02:04:21.828
Magneto.

1489
02:04:22.305 --> 02:05:22.287
-== [ www.OpenSubtitles.org ] ==-
